The Prague Stock Exchange finished with fewer points at the end of the day
After the rapid fall of the morning, the Prague Stock Exchange corrected its losses.
ČEZ’s stock transactions reached about half the value they have on a normal day.
The Prague Stock Exchange, at the beginning of commercial Tuesday, reacted immediately to Monday’s fall when it fell to approximately 6%.
The decline this time is due to the falling stocks on Wall Street.
Also here is the reaction of the market to the result of the vote of the American Assembly of Representatives that refused to support the stabilization plan of the secretary of the financial sector.
Declining Stocks in Asia
Shares of the Asian stocks experienced a dramatic decline on Tuesday, albeit over the course of the day the index finally mitigated some of the losses.
Hong Kong’s Hang Seng stock index during its financial day scored nearly four percent, though it later mitigated its losses by reducing the decline by nearly 2.5 percent.
Hang Seng’s China Enterprises index that tracks Chinese stock movements on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange fell 3.8 percent in Shanghai markets were closed.
Sidney’s stock lost more than five percent but, in the end, losses fell to 4.3 percent.
The Taiwan Stock Exchange according to the index secretary fell to 3.6 percent.
“Scheduled bailout shares in the U.S. are unsafe and this influences the financial market around the world,” Hong Kong Currency Bureau Chief Joseph Yam said.
Although Hong Kong is a part of China, it only determines its monetary policy, that is, without dependence on the Central Bank of China.
Hong Kong’s interest rates are at the same level as those in the United States.
U.S. legislators should reconvene as soon as possible, according to Australian Prime Minister Kevin Rudd, and approve a proposal to support the financial system.
In another way, it threatens that the falls will be felt in other countries.
Bloody Bath of American Stocks
On Monday, the American Assembly of Representatives rejected the financial aid plan to which 700 billion dollars (almost 12 trillion kroners) should be dedicated.
Legislators, in that way, ignored President George Bush’s invitation to support his plan.
For Bush, the plan would solve the root causes of the financial crisis and help stabilize the entire economy.
On Monday, U.S. stocks experienced a bloody bath and mainly the stock index picked up the biggest drop in more than 20 years.
The Dow Jones index fell to nearly seven percent. A similar volume drop was last recorded in 1987.
The index already fell before being announced but as soon it was shown that the proposal of the assembly did not go ahead, the index began to fall freely.
Congress withdrew: The U.S. government can inject 700 billion dollars into banking
The highest representatives of Congress and the administration, President George W. Bush, agreed on a pact on broad terms of financial aid to the American finance system.
Their vote will take place early next week.
U.S
However, it is not yet won.
Congresters must fine-tune some details of the contract before they can make the final form of the law public and be voted on.
The financial aid plan will be discussed Monday in the Assembly of Representatives.
Barney Frank, chairman of the Committee for Financial Services and Assembly Banking, told Reuters on Sunday.
According to some sources, the vote on the plan could take place in the Senate no earlier than Wednesday.
According to economists, the arrival of ratification of the rescue plan should represent the announcement of a psychologically significant first factor for the revitalization of the financial market.
Then, however, "disenchantment" will be achieved thanks to the complex mechanisms whose market aid will also reach in practice.
Paulson: The plan needs to be effective
“We made a breakthrough.
We fixed our dissenting views regarding how the market stabilization measures package should have," Democrat Nancy Pelosiá told Bloomberg.
According to her, the final vote could still take place on Sunday.
Legislators gathered Sunday night with Finance Minister Henry Paulson to give a definitive form to the Government Fund.
It should buy from financial companies unsolded mortgage assets that lead financial companies to severe losses and threaten the stability of the entire system.
"We are about to close the agreement on the plan, which will work and will also need to be effective in the market.
We still need to continue with the sanitation plan, but I think we’re already on it,” Paulson said.
A Sign for Asian Businesses
The global financial crisis has an explicit impact on the rapidly declining stock market.
According to Democratic Nevada Senator Harry Reid, lawmakers are doing everything they can to get Congress to finally pass a deal Sunday.
They thus want to reassure investors’ businesses before the Asian financy market since these are those that are in the first time zone and where Congress could influence trade on Monday.
However, for now there is nothing clear with certainty about when the two chambers of the U.S. congressional will vote and, not even, if they will not stagnate at the last moment with a problem.
Legislators believe it will be approved in the coming days.
The law, however, will undergo a series of changes.
The total amount intended to help the system must be divided into two parts.
The first 350 billion must be available as soon as possible, as President George Bush requested.
However, Congress can block the release of the remaining amount if it had the impression that the program does not fulfill its function, which would concern another 100 billion dollars and, later, the last 350 billion dollars.
Bush appreciated the progress of the meetings
On the other hand, the president can veto this decision but the Congress can overcome his veto by a majority of votes.
Despite these changes, the basic idea of the program that consisted of earning financial resources for the repurchase of bad mortgage securities whose value fell because hundreds of thousands of Americans are not able to finish paying their mortgages.
“We’ve worked everything.
The Assembly of Representatives would have to be prepared to vote the law on Sunday, and the Senate on Monday," Republican Senator Judd Gregg said.
Also U.S. President Bush is pleased with the progress of the meetings.
His spokesman, Tony Fratto, announced that Bush is satisfied with Saturday's progress and values "the commitment of both sides to stabilize our financial market and protect our economy."
Constraining the armored contract
Senate Banking Committee Chairman Christopher Dodd said lawmakers have decided on responsibility for the taxpayer’s tax-supprising money for their losses, a spill-over closure of the scheduled finance plan.
The new law should also limit so-called armoured contracts for directors of the participating companies of the program, and it creates a committee that will have control of the Fund.
The Ministry of Finances would have to run it.
"We've worked very hard on it, and we've made a breakthrough towards the convention that will work and that will be effective for the market and for all Americans," Paulson said.
The plan also counts on helping homeowners who have problems with their payments.
The government would have to agree with the new mortgage payments it purchases in order to lower the monthly burdens of debtors’ installment payments and allow them to keep their homes.
Marek: psychological help
The proposed plan is, according to the chief economist of Patria Finance, David Marek, a good idea that will be made but quite difficult.
"And that's why we don't know what mechanism and at what price the problematic assets will be bought.
This will be decisive for the distribution of losses between the financial sector and the government," Marek told server iHNed.cz this week.
That the plan is approved now or early next week is not, according to Marek, so relevant.
"Much more importantly, already this week the congressmen agree on their support and give their approval as soon as possible.
This important and psychological agreement that that approval will be reached is, at the moment, the most important thing," Marek insisted.
Armed hand fight: the MP3 player against the mobile.
We advise you how to choose
While almost every phone plays MP3 files, no MP3 player can make calls.
Which seems clear that it’s better to buy just the phone.
Even so, there are enough reasons for the man to acquire only the player.
The choice practically depends on the manner of its use and the demand of the future owner.
It will probably be difficult for him to acquire the most modern turntables to listen to Maxim Turbulenc’s latest album.
On the other hand, this type of musical products such as LP albums no longer come out, and in terms of their quality there is not a single objective reason to keep buying them.
If vinyl records are crowded on your shelves with art rock, jazz or blues music, you’re probably dreaming, at least, of this type of turntable.
This is the same with the music that is on its way, i.e. the compressed, simplified music - the music in MP3.
There are categories of price and quality here.
For some it may be unacceptable to spend eight thousand crowns on a player, just like for a Pink Floyd lover who will hardly test twenty-krone market hulls.
Two ends, between which there is enough space for each.
The choice is wide.
It also decides the battery life
Some of the best players achieve much more than just playing music and even what not even most phones.
No current device is as universal as the phone.
Faced with the most elementary functions such as telephoning, sending messages, you can play music and video, record both, have a better or worse photography device and you can even navigate.
And when we take into consideration the Smartphone and the PDAs are going to have a small computer in their pocket as well.
This is a small miracle since no refrigerator knows how to make a barbecue and no television can photograph.
The universality of mobiles also brings us disadvantages.
The more functions you use on the mobile before the display indicator will illuminate asking to be recharged.
And music playback is one of the biggest traces of energy.
There are few phones that manage to play music more than ten or twelve hours, most much less.
In this sense, music players (especially the simplest ones) clearly have higher performance.
Therefore, keep in mind that cheap phones will not play more than two hours.
If in addition to this, on top of it, they constantly get themselves still, for more security, a charger for the job - this is also valid for the most expensive appliances.
With the MP3 player this problem will not have it, as even the worst endure at least 9 hours of uninterrupted operation after a load.
Another problem happens when recording music on mobile.
Unfortunately, only a part of the devices has the universal USB connector and, in addition, not all of them can be connected directly to the computer without special software.
Of course it is possible to record music directly on the memory card but only in some unreduced reading units can the small memory cards that are used in mobiles can be connected.
In players, with some exception (iPod), no special software is necessary.
It is enough to fill the device with music through the USB of the computer.
Most phones and players create their order alone in the music library according to the name of the performer, album title, genre or also according to user rating.
Some devices only show a directory with a tree structure similar to a Windows Finder and some recognize both (iriver, Samsung, Sony, Cowon, smartphones with operating system).
The player tries to serve, the phone knows more
For the choice of a specific team, to be interested in the resistance of the accumulator, for the capacity of the memory, for the quality and type of sound output and, of course, for the convenience of its handling.
If you listen, above all, the music as a background and you will listen to it every day only for a while, as in the tram, then it is enough with any mobile that plays.
What practically really achieves any mobile.
You shouldn't even be interested in the format in which your phone or player plays the music.
The MP3 is played by everyone and, practically, almost all the music that reaches it will be in this format.
It is among the most widespread and excluding him the absolute majority of the devices play music in WMA format.
Those less include the AAC format (format used by the Apple company and its iPod).
The best phones also make it possible, for example, to buy music online.
It is enough through the mobile internet to visit the competent pages of the operator (or of any other service provider) and buy a song or an album.
This service alone could be a compelling argument to acquire a mobile for music.
Unfortunately the supply of operators is miserable and the majority is limited only to the fucking-success issues of radios.
Prices aren't the lowest either.
However, in general, it is assumed that precisely this way of selling music (whether by GSM, internet or wireless internet) in the future will dominate the music industry.
Most people always carry a cell phone.
Whenever you want to hear something, you’ll find your phone in your pocket, while the MP3 player will be forgotten at home.
However, it still depends on whether you’re always wearing headphones or, at least, handsfree.
If not, you can use a built-in player that has virtually every phone even if it’s at least an MP3 player.
Probably the biggest advantage for many mobiles with music will be their price.
The cheapest usually cost less than three thousand.
Between three and four thousand kroners you can already acquire a good walkman.
Most of you will limit the absence of an input for classic headphones.
The best, even when it comes to the technical part, such as phones equipped with an input of 3.5 mm. for classic headphones, cost up to fifteen thousand.
Again, the advantage of the players is nothing more than their easy service.
The simplest players – by no means necessarily the cheapest ones (see our selection) – are actually handled by anyone.
The minimum functions, their handling similar to the previous ordinary cassettes or also the turntables is evident.
It does not represent a threat in the sense that by mistake we connect to the internet with the mobile and, consequently, gigantic account by data decline.
For which apparatus to decide
Even the cheapest phones (e.g. Vodafone 527) generally have a slot to change the memory card (type M2, micro SD, etc.).
Even with the purchase of a suitable card you will reach two thousand kroner.
However, be careful.
The basic models are usually equipped only with a 2 GB card of maximum capacity.
Only the most expensive have an 8 GB memory.
If you already have a mobile and still want to buy a cheap MP3 player, take a look at Cowon, Creativ, Sony, Samsung, Emgeton or Iriver.
Depending on capacity (at most 2 GB) there is no need to spend more than 1,100 kroners.
If you consider among the most demanding music lovers take advantage of the most specialized mobile-walkman (Sony Ericsson, some Nokia and Samsung).
These devices have independent keys for the MP3 which makes a service as comfortable as that of the same player.
The most specialized of all is Sony Ericsson, whose mobiles of the walkman line have almost identical use as that of a standalone MP3 player.
The same service and the same category in terms of price, over four thousand crowns, but with a greater memory capacity (up to 16 GB) and accumulator (normally 15 hours, with a maximum yield of up to 35 hours), the brand cited more arria brings them MP3 players.
The first virtual operator will arrive, this year, in the Czech Republic.
It'll probably
The mobile market in the Czech Republic is fairly developed and our operators offer virtually all services as their Western European partners.
However, here we still lack something - the virtual operator, which would force those to be cheaper.
It's probably not going to take long to arrive.
That the Czech operators are part of the most expensive in Europe, we have already written it on mobil.cz.
The rest was also confirmed by the Czech Telecommunications Office (ČTÚ) which warned that the price of SMS messages in our country is one of the most expensive in the Union.
Following the European Commission’s final steps in the field of roaming rate regulation it will probably come into a paradoxical situation - for some customers of Czech mobile operators the SMS they sent from abroad will be cheaper than if sent from home.
How is it possible for prices in the Czech Republic to remain so high compared to Europe?
The answer is simple, there is a lack of competition that really wants to fight.
This is probably paradoxical, because we have three mobile networks and their high coverage is more than 100%.
By contrast, mobile operators like to lament that there is extreme competition in the Czech market.
That is also the President of the Council of the Czech Telecommunications Office (ČTÚ), Pavel Dvořák, already expressed that there is no longer room in the Czech Republic for any other operator.
It is perhaps true that for a classic operator with its own network it no longer has too many possibilities (for the rest, it would be very difficult to find some frequency).
However, there’s still a possibility – the virtual operator.
Precisely the entry of the virtual operator into the mobile phone market brought a significant decrease in prices against which the classic operators also had to react.
At the same time, even before the entry of sharks such as Tesco Mobile or Virgin Mobile to the British market, similar voices were heard both there and here.
It was showned that there is room for such operators and that they can be successful.
Otherwise, you don’t need to look for examples too far.
In February of this year we informed you about the premiere of the virtual operator Mobilking in Poland.
Only after half a year, this operator managed to obtain more than 100 thousand customers and become the fifth largest operator in the neighboring country.
On the other hand, after Mobilking is the Penta group that, apart from this, in the Czech Republic is the owner of U:fon.
The advantage of virtual operators is the possibility to focus on many more specific target groups.
In addition, in order for them to function effectively, it is enough for many fewer customers than a classic operator.
They do not carry relatively large expenses in construction, operation and maintenance of the network.
In the world this type of virtual operators are usually profiled with low expenses - they offer cheap SMS calls and messages that however, is often counterrested with the offer of tighter services.
Thus, for example, Tesco mobile in Great Britain offers SMS at least half cheap compared to the competition.
However, as the example of Mobilking in Poland shows, it can also be a good blow to the bet for a nothing trivial target group.
This operator specifically targets man.
“The right man chooses Mobilking — it’s the operator who likes and who can be trusted,” says David Seibert, the CEO of Mobile Entertainment Company, who works this virtual operator.
It’s hard to say whether a concept like Poland could engage in our country.
Vodafone spokesman Miroslav Čepický said: "The Czech market is relatively small to access by segments on which the majority of virtual operators are based.
In addition from the point of view of the offer of services is relatively saturated"
In the Czech Republic there is no chance, mobile operators say
However, it seems almost certain that if in the Czech Republic there will be some virtual operator that will not be Mobilking.
"We're talking about the expansion of this successful project, however, in R. Checa doesn't seem too hopeful.
Rather it’s the launch of Mobilking in other countries in our region,” Jana Studničková, a spokesman for the financial group Penta, said in a telephone conversation for mobil.cz.
He indirectly assured that the current mobile operators in the Czech Republic definitely do not bow to this idea.
On the contrary, they try to do everything possible so that no potential competition arises.
Interest on the launch of a virtual mobile operator is already shown by the GTS Novera group that would like to take a step further to become a real Telefónica O2 competition in the field of business customers.
"We have a great interest in this, in order to be able to offer our customers not only fixed telephony services but also mobile telephony services.
And how much earlier, the better.
With this possibility, we have repeatedly encountered all Czech mobile carriers.
With some of them we have managed to advance in the meetings," group spokesman Pavel Kaidl said.
Then maybe they'll flash better times.
It seems that, by unofficial information, the first official operator would possibly have to arrive by the end of the year.
But for now its appearance is accompanied by an impenetrable wall of silence.
"Right now we believe that the situation is ideal for the emergence of a virtual operator in the Czech market.
The Czech market compared to others is a very specific market.
So far no one has addressed us with any complex and serious project in this field, "said for mobil.cz, Vlastimil Sršeň, spokesman for Telefónica O2.
Other operators are referred to the specificity of the Czech market.
T-mobile spokeswoman Martina Kemrová, in exceptional accordance with O2's opinion, adds: "Until today we have not registered any viable commercial project that, bilaterally profitable, can continue to develop."
"On the T-Mobile network it will be difficult to find a virtual operator until the end of the year.
At the moment we should already have on the table some concrete contract that it was possible to study in such a short horizon
Vodafone directs your attention rather to the fulfilment of the requirements of a 3G license.
Miroslav Čepický adds: "We are open for negotiations with potential virtual operators, and this in terms of spending and infrastructure sharing.
Precisely we consider it as the greatest contribution from the point of view of customers.
Vodafone’s main strategy in this field lies in the partner with whom to establish a shared network for a fast internet on mobile.”
Responsible offices - with operators nail and meat
The progress of mobile operators can be easily understood, but the entry of another operator would mean increasing competition which would lead to a drop in prices and thus a decrease in earnings.
So why make it easier to enter the competition?
When operators want to get something, they are able to pull the same rope, proof of this is the grip when U:fon emerged.
Perhaps the biggest pressure on ČTÚ was at the time of U:fon’s entry by T-Mobile.
This is attested to public information accessible on ČTÚ’s websites.
But precisely now U:fon serves as an argument of why not to accept a virtual operator.
Martina Kemrová adds to this: "In addition, the competitive environment in the mobile telephony market was open to a fourth operator.
With regard to the nature of the mobile telephony market in the Czech Republic, it is natural that the entry of another player into the market would mean for him and, above all, for his services great requirements."
This is why this access to mobile operators is tremendously discouraging due to the absolute disinterest of the Czech regulatory body.
It’s not just about ČTU’s stance, which unfortunately has no competence to intervene in trade tenders, unlike Britain and other developed countries.
This belongs purely to the Office for the Protection of Commercial Bidding (ÚOHS).
However, it expressed its typical position on this problem.
"Entry of a virtual operator into the mobile market would be possible after an agreement was concluded on the rental of the necessary infrastructure between a mobile operator and a virtual operator.
Until today, no agreement has been closed since the offer of potential stakeholders rather was not interesting enough for classic operators," Kristián Chalupa, from the ÚOHS foreign relations department, added to our question.
These statements are not surprising to the representatives of the operators.
For the offices that must represent the interests of consumers it is more than a consideration, apart from this they must observe that no one takes advantage of their position in the market.
Especially when Kristián Chalupa adds: "Abroad where virtual operators operate normally we can see that their entry into the market contributed to the drop in prices of mobile phone services"
Obviously, the pressure on the proper functioning of market means and the fall in prices does not fall within the interest of the UOHS.
Truly the dramatically shocking in all of this case lies in the dissonating reactions that result from the three mobile operators.
The question of whether it is really a coincidence is offered by itself.
It is the same as with the price of gasoline at gas stations because it is clear that it is the work of chance and a hard struggle for competition.
"The Office in this regard has found no signs of unfair competition and has therefore no reason to intervene.
None of the operators has a dominant position, therefore, they do not have a corresponding increase in responsibility in their actions in the market.
The tools necessary to open up the mobile phone market to virtual operators, rather missing, as well as telecommunications regulators," Chalupa added.
The interpretation of the dominant position in the market is one of many conflicting points.
Obviously there is a relevant market analysis prepared by ČTÚ according to which telecommunications are from the point of view of the commercial tendering a single market.
In this type of market naturally none of the Czech traders has a dominant position.
However some of the legal experts offer another view - for a virtual operator to arise it is always necessary the agreement with the network administrator.
And the operator of mobile telephony - with all its logic - has a monopoly on its network.
Therefore, in a specific segment it must necessarily be dominant.
And if this argument were not accepted, at least for ÚOHS it should represent a warning the fact that three mobile operators ascend strikingly in a similar way.
The current complaints of the interested parties (including the aforementioned company GTS Novera) show that in all negotiations with the operators they clash with many similar impediments.
Carrying responsibility in ČTÚ is a fairly common trick in the field of telecommunications from which the ÚOHS washes its hands in this whole matter.
We've met him already in some similar cases.
Unfortunately recently, a new amendment to the telecommunications law for the extension of ČTÚ’s competence in the field of commercial tenders was tabled, even though a number of specialists promised that the situation would improve.
ÚOHS representatives should know this perfectly well, but it is clear that their interests lie elsewhere.
It's all right, when nobody watches
At the same time, unnoticedly something like a pseudo-virtual operator is still functioning that in Czech mobile telephone networks there are already a few.
They are companies that put their own prices to mobile phone services which, however, only a part are public.
Normally these are companies that are dedicated to multilevel marketing.
Amway, Bohemia Telecom, Starlife and many offer their own mobile telephony services.
Normally only a few chosen get the price list of these companies.
The magic is that the company, with respect to the operator, acts as a classic business customer of the same commissioning a lot of SIM cards.
As a special customer you will then receive special prices and other offers.
The problem is that trading conditions in all Czech mobile operators prohibit such resale.
"If cases such as those cited could be discovered, one could speak of infringement in the conditions of contract that could result in the end of collaboration with the given society," Martina Kemrová responded to the question about this problem.
But it is quite unlikely that an activity of this type carried out by mobile operators did not reach responsible people.
Precisely in the case of the three companies cited, it can become thousands of customers.
None of the operators are against this procedure.
With the activities of these companies they make no despicable profits and, at the same time - unlike authentic virtual operators - in no way threaten their own official marketing.
Miroslav Čepický warns us of the possible problems: "the law allows speculation of this type, however, the services of this company are used only by a negligible percentage of customers.
They must also accept that their phone’s SIM card is not in their name so they can’t absolutely dispose of it as a normal carrier customer.”
Precisely this is what it should seem to ČTÚ minimally strange.
In addition, a new question for the UOHS appears.
If mobile operators turn their eyes on this type of procedure, why do they block the virtual operator’s input?
It is necessary to add that the ÚOHS has enough competence to discover this type of activities and if it will not want to be content with the explanations of the operators that they have no idea of this history and that their commercial conditions do not allow it.
When we'll stop being the most expensive
As was already clear in the text, the entry of the virtual operator into the mobile phone market led to a significant decrease in service prices.
At the same time, in virtually all the countries where the virtual operator emerged, classical operators tried more or less to protect themselves from this disruption.
The arguments used by these were practically all identical - too small, a market, eventually too saturated, problems with the quality of service, etc.
In the most advanced countries, however, the regulatory bodies have intervened at the moment and in none of the cases defended the operators but their customers.
Whether with formal measures or informal pressure, they managed to raise the first virtual operator and with it began to emerge others.
Unfortunately, the Czech Regulatory Organ all this case happens as if it were a burning nail.
From our experience we cannot fail to be impressed that the confusion of attributions in these cases suits them.
But don’t despair.
If this behind-the-scenes information is correct and the virtual operator actually arrives on these lands, then the Czech mobile market is likely to start moving again.
If any of the operators let some virtual telephony operator enter, it will be difficult for the UOHS to remain indifferent to the rejection (discrimination) of other stakeholders.
And maybe we’ll stop calling more expensive than in the rest of Europe.
The new Czech anthem has four new versions.
Choose the best
Hear all four presentations of the new version of the official Czech anthem.
On Sunday, Prime Minister Mirek Topolánek on the occasion of the day of the official Czech celebrations presented the new official recording of the anthem Where, my home.
The new anthem was recorded by the National Theatre orchestra under the direction of Jiří Bělohlávek.
There are available four versions - two versions that are Solos, one by male voice and one with female voice, another with Choir and another instrumental.
Kateřina Kněžínková and Adam Plachetka are in charge of singing.
The authors of the anthem arrangements are Otakar Jeremiáš and Jaroslav Krček.
On the iHNed.cz server you can listen to all four versions.
Bělohlavek regards this Czech national song as one of the most beautiful hymns.
The Czech Radio already said earlier that it intentionally chose for the Singer Solos with representatively young voices that are more expressive and popular.
"From the beginning I have tried with the two and then, also, with the Choir to look at the diction so that the text would be well understood, so that it would be consistent," he said.
The official Czech anthem celebrates its 175th anniversary next year.
The song Where, my Home sounded for the first time in 1834 on the boards of the Theatre of the States in the original Czech work Fidlovačka by Josef Kajetán Tyl and arranged with the music of František Škroup.
It gained popularity and people made it their own.
The first verse of the song after the rise of Czechoslovakia in 1918 naturally became a part of the official anthem.
One of the seven official symbols remained even after the emergence of the independent Czech Republic.
How "new" hymn sounds
The MHD in Prague takes us on Wednesday for the first time with the chip
On Wednesday, October 1, 2008, it is written in the history of the Prague Transport Company the date on which the first passengers enter the subway, the tram and the bus with an electronic voucher in their pockets instead of a paper ticket.
This can currently be acquired by almost one hundred thousand people who own the Opencard chip card.
Passengers can purchase the 30-day, 90-day and annual voucher (this will be validated from 1 January 2009) and simultaneously charge it on their chip card at the infocenters and transport company stalls at Metro stations, Muzeum, Můstek, Nádraží Holešovice, Anděl, Roztyly, Letňany, Kobylisy
Bonds can already be purchased from yesterday on the Internet on the pages of the transport company, www.dpp.cz.
The service, until the afternoon, was used by more than four hundred people.
Those who start using the internet as a form of commerce, can definitely begin to forget about ticket stalls at subway stations, where until now they should regularly queue up to take out a normal ticket.
The voucher is purchased on the Internet, and the Opencard card is recharged in one of the thirteen subsidiaries of the Municipal Library.
"In these places there is available to passengers a window with prepared personnel that helps those interested with the online purchase and also with the recharging of the voucher bought on their card," said the spokesman of the project, Martin Opatrný.
Apart from the library, it will also be possible to recharge the electronic bonus in the Opencard in the automatic vending machines that are located in some metro lobbies.
How are these vending machines?
They are red, they remind us of a banknote riding machine and travelers will probably have already noticed them in the metro stations of Roztyly, Budějovická, I. P. Pavlova, Florenc and Vltavská.
"There are now five in the city but at the end of the year there would have to be eighty," Opatrný completed.
The bonus is controlled by the machine rather than the driver
The use of the machine, which will begin to work tomorrow, is simple.
It is enough to enter the Opencard chip card in it and the previously paid bonus will be uploaded only on it.
The electronic bonds from tomorrow are valid not only in the capital but also in its surroundings.
That is to say, on ring road trains and bus lines from the numbers 300 to 499 that mainly use the inhabitants of the towns of central Bohemia.
"In the trains attached to the integrated transport of Prague there are reviewers equipped with a reading card that will help confirm the validity of the time and area of the voucher," explained the control of the tickets, Filip Drápal of the Ropid organization that establishes the schedules of the collective transport of Prague.
The bypass buses have their reader cards mounted on the driver's locker.
When entering it is necessary not only to show the card to the driver but it is also necessary to accompany it with the Opencard in the place destined for it on the side of the Box.
With this, the driver controls the validity of the bonus.
"If the passenger needs to verify the validity of the bonuses there is nothing easier than to ask the driver for this information," Drápal said.
Passengers who do not travel on bypass buses and do not remember when it is terminated the validity of the voucher can go to vending machines where the cards are recharged.
Here, on the machine screen, you will be shown the information about the validity of your document.
The Southeast wanted to be part of the U.S. in a referendum
The German Sweats asked in 1945 that Fumaba be part of the United States.
This is what is extracted from the letter that is kept in the collection of the Southern Bohemian Scientific Library.
If we cannot be part of Germany or Austria, we at least want to live under the United States.
With this desire, presumably some groups of Germans from the Sudetes were addressed to the president of the U.S. in 1945.
It results from the letters that are kept in a particular archive and that today are kept in the collection of the Scientific Library of Bohemia of the South.
Český Krumlov’s Germans request in a letter to the American president not to allow the return of the “Šumava land” – occupied by Hitler based on the Munich Pact – back to Czechoslovakia.
"We have correctly understood the situation and we really want their word that the American units are coming to German lands not as oppressors or enemies but as liberators" is written in the letter, signed with a "the people who carry the fate of Šumava in their heart."
Given that Czechoslovakia’s union with the Germans presumably supposes – according to them the Czech national character – a hope only in brutality, disregard, misunderstanding, pressure and slavery, the authors pray in the letter to the American president to assume Šumava for today and forever under a protectorate.
"We cannot believe that without considering the opinion of four million inhabitants it gives us to a foreign state that oppresses and rejects minorities and that it at all collaborates with the victory of the allies," the letter wrote.
The reason why authors cannot sign is presumably the fear of "Czech oppressors" reprisals.
If the U.S. president presumably hesitated about this idea of šumavo Germans, it would suffice to organize in the šumavas lands a referendum on whether its inhabitants want to be part of the U.S
Although the text of the letter, with the knowledge that we have today of post-war history, it may sound a little childish, according to some specialists it paints the expectations of the Germans of the south-easters at the time.
Although the Czech Germans had to minimally intuify that his expulsion from the republic was to be dealt with only a few admitted this possibility.
Some hoped that the United States and Great Britain would negotiate for the Sudetes some clear form of autonomy.
Others believed they would stay in Czechoslovakia.
It is confirmed even by the Austrian journalist Gustav Chalupa, born in České Budějovice.
He was in the war, as German of Budějovice, rooted in the Baltic navy.
When at the end of the war the Britons seized him and placed him in Holstein’s prison camp dozens of Germans went to him to teach them Czech.
"They believed that when they returned home, the Czech would use it," Chalupa said.
None of the German prisoners who lived before the war in Czechoslovakia, according to him, said that based on the Decrees of Benes they would be removed from the Republic.
You don't thint - you pay!
Emotive Campaign Attacks Drivers
The most expensive action in Czech history aimed at road safety.
In this way it could characterize the emotive Campaign that the Ministry of Transport in the media decided to launch on Wednesday.
Minister’s office, Aleš Řebíček, promises that he will deter drivers from dangerous behaviour behind the wheel.
The 150 million campaign will be felt in television, radio, cinema, the internet and in leaflets.
It would have to deter the driver from high speed and alcohol behind the wheel.
And also to remind them that before they get going the belts.
He wants to reach awareness especially of young drivers, motorcyclists, pedestrians and in the last place also of professional drivers.
And what can we see in advertisements?
Fundamentally human histories that ram into emotions.
And for this we are witnessed by the "bleeding" announcements throughout the campaign:
You don't thint - you pay!
The word "Don't think" is written in large letters on the license plate.
And in a puddle of blood is the word "paid."
This must symbolise that man in a moment of layoff can come to pay with his own life.
Ads are going to “scare” viewers until 2010.
The Ministry was inspired by the campaign carried out in Anglo-Saxon lands where strong images of victims of accidents can be observed.
It promises that that way it will reduce accidents and the death toll on Czech roads.
The announcements have been produced by Euro RSCG.
Sugar and Whip for Drivers
"For drivers it's worth the sugar and whip system.
Sugar is for him when, for example, a red traffic light is passed and thus saves time.
The whip is a threat of a fine or accident.
Drivers must be reminded of the risks," says Na Homolce hospital transportation psychologist Martin Kořán.
And that’s why it’s necessary an information campaign in the press and mainly a negative publicity, the psychologist specifies.
Less effective, for him, are the panels that warn the driver of the dangers.
"If there is any panel installed warning of some danger it will probably soon merge with the environment and the driver will not pay greater attention to it," Kořán warned.
Olmert would return almost all occupied areas in exchange for peace
The president of the provisional government of Israel, Ehud Olmert, spoke about the restitution of virtually all lands occupied in 1967, i.e. the West Bank, East Jerusalem and the Golan Heights, in exchange for peace with Palestinians and Syria.
He proposed in the interview that on Monday he appeared in the Yedioth Ahronoth newspaper.
"We must reach an agreement with the Palestinians which means that we will necessarily have to restore almost all (occupied) land if not all," Olmert told the newspaper.
"Surely we'll take some percent of these lands, but to the Palestinians we will have to cede a similar percent (of Israel's lands) because without this there will be no peace."
He admitted that in case of restitution East Jerusalem would also be included.
"Whoever wants security in Jerusalem and therefore doesn't want tractors or bulldozers to pass over his legs as happened to one of my best friends, then he will have to hand over a part of Jerusalem," Olmert said, referring to the two July attacks in the city in which several people were killed and dozens were injured.
According to the president it will be necessary to find "a special solution for Temple Hill, sacred and historical place" that is located inside the ancient city.
"Whoever wants to maintain Israeli sovereignty throughout the city will have to integrate 270,000 Arabs.
This won't work," he insisted later.
Golan Height Retiring
Olmert also spoke for Israel’s withdrawal from the Golan Heights, which from his point of view is an inherent condition for closing a peace agreement with Syria.
But this would also entail concrete efforts by Damascus.
"I do not intend to close peace with Syria solely on the basis of the Golan's withdrawal," he warned.
"Syrians know well what they will have to detach from in order to win the Golan.
They will have to abandon their current relations with Iran, they must abandon their relations with Hezbollah (Chita movement), they must divest themselves of the permanent support caused by Hamas (Chita movement), al Qaeda (the terrorist network) and Jihad (the Holy War) in Iraq.
Questions after the accident: Are hostesses illegal on buses?
The law is unfamiliar, you can't walk on a long-distance bus
In relation to the tragic accident of the Student Agency bus near the Italian city of Padova, the question arises as to whether hostesses and passengers can move around the bus during the trip.
“If we wanted to strictly and formally comply with the law, hostess activity is opposed to the road traffic law,” Transportation Ministry spokesman Karel Hanzelka says.
The accident in which the twenty-two-year-old hostess died last week was evidently caused by the driver of the truck only that the bus crossed the road.
The girl, unfortunately, was sitting next to the driver in the less safe place of the vehicle despite having reserved another two places.
However, the bus may have an accident or brake suddenly, and at the precise moment when the stewardess distributes coffee or newspapers.
Here what the role plays is if the bus is endowed, according to the technical permission, with walking places.
If the bus is not approved, the passenger must be seated.
Student Agency’s long-distance buses have no places to step, which the company’s director, Radim Jančura, confirmed at Aktuálně.cz.
“We’ve sorted this out with the ministry and, in principle, the movement of passengers is not allowed.
Finally this was withdrawn and we reached the agreement that passengers can go to the bathroom while the bus is running if they have a seat, "he told us his position.
The hostess doesn't know the law
“There is no obvious legal interpretation of the role of hostess – no legal provision clarifies this function.
Not even any legal provision prohibits transport agents from performing any service.
“Road transport law only knows the term Vehicle Reviewer, whose rights and obligations are undefined,” spokesman Hanzelka said.
The director of the Department of Road Vehicle Traffic of the Ministry of Transport, Josef Pokorný, thinks on the contrary that the law sufficiently addresses this problem.
"Depends on whether the bus has the approval allowed to have walking sites.
That's it," he says.
Buses are divided between the city, where there are places to stand and limited maximum speed, interurban with places to stand with a greater speed permit and those of long distances without places to go standing, with the greatest speed permit and with seats equipped with seat belts.
Just like on the plane, the expert says
BESIP’s transport safety expert, Jaroslav Hořín, sees no major issues regarding the movement of hostess on the bus.
"During the development of the voyage there is not much threat of danger, the situation can be compared to service on airplanes.
Even here you don’t have the assurance that the turbulences will arrive and that the hostess can be hit in the head.”
"However, if the bus suddenly suddenly brakes that physical laws are valid.
Same as in a city bus or on the tram.
The safety of hostesses must solve the internal regulations of the carrier," he says and also thinks that from the point of view of the law this problem is unsolved.
Jančura is ready to cancel this service
Student Agency is the only carrier to offer hostess service.
He employs two hundred in it.
The director, not even after the accident, considers that risky job.
“However, the moment I have the impression that the hostess position is risky, then I’ll suppress it.
Coffee and newspapers can receive it, passengers, upon entering.
It would save even expenses," he says.
Interesting to safety is why Asiana lacks hostesses in her vehicles, according to Alexej Litvin, who runs a small line compared to SA.
"We don't have hostesses, we're against them from the beginning.
Sooner or later this will end in a deadly accident," he said less than a year ago for Týden.cz.
An enormous tragedy happened
In the accident of the line that connects to Naples, a young stewardess from Pilsen who had worked for the company two years died.
A Slovene truck that likely turned from the parking lane blocking the passage to the bus without using intermittents.
His driver tried in a quick manoeuvre to avoid it, however, it collided with the front right.
Jančura denies that the two sites that are reserved for the hostess rest were sold.
“These sites are not possible to reserve them for long-distance connections, they are blocked.”
The company intends to sue the truck driver.
The agency will not wait for the verdict of the trial on the compensation of the girl's family but awaits the financial expenses also by the part of the culprit.
Reform of the law?
No, for now
The reform of the law could bring greater precision about the movement of hostesses on the bus in which for a year that thirty experts members of a group of the Ministry of Transport have been working.
"However, they have not reached any concrete conclusions.
They are not too dedicated to the buses, but rather to the system of points, maximum speed on the highway and the use of the mobile during the march, "says expert Hořín.
"The Ministry of Transport does not consider the activity of hostesses something that significantly threatens the safety of passengers," spokesman Hanzelka concluded that the control of safety in the buses is the responsibility of the police and the Office of Safety at work.
Dusseldorf's hope is supported by Frankfurt
In the letter of the board of directors of West LB for his collaborators there is no shortage of great words.
Due to the merger of Dusseldorf’s units with the DEKA bank “a central capital market of Sparkassen’s financial group”, as the letter says, published on Monday
West LB, breaking the ‘competition block’ with sustainable earning capacity would go into such a business.
In addition, such a merger may be a beginning for subsequent mergers in the field of regional banks.
This is how he comes to understand the text, when a board of directors wants to show the ability to act in hard times.
'Cause just like the West LB is under enormous pressure before.
Not only from the part of the European Union, but also from the federal financial services surveillance institute that has recently made it clear to the government of the North-Westphalia that there is little time left to find a solution.
For some time now, also on the Frankfurt side, there has been a lot of talk about the union of such a kind between the DEKA bank, which Sparkasse clients know for their investment funds, and the West LB.
Indeed, Franz Waas, the head of the DEKA bank, presenting the data after a half-year at the end of August let him know that he does not see any sense in the merger of the bank, located on Mainzer Straße Street, with a regional bank such as Helaba or West LB.
But DEKA’s board of directors, which is now made up of regional banks and Sparkassen’s associations, commissioned the board of directors to begin negotiations with the West LB on common business activities.
In this it could be a business in the capital market or parts of it.
Of course, the negotiations have just begun, that's how it's said on the financial site.
It is not the first time when it comes to the consolidation in Sparkassen’s area the name of the DEKA bank that with its 3000 collaborators is among the most important entrepreneurs on the financial site Frankfurt.
In 2003 at one point the situation thus seemed that DEKA bank could merge with the regional bank of Rhineland-Palatinate and with Helaba.
This initiative to create a three-party uninception was left without results.
Hardly the plans were made public, the Hesse government expressed itself against Helaba’s participation in this project.
The other two banks also didn’t find the same language.
Instead, the regional bank of the Rhineland-Palatinate began the dialogue with the regional bank of Baden-Württemberg.
But it was always played again with the idea of merging the DEKA bank with other regional banks.
But finally Günther Merl, the chairman of Helaba’s board of directors, said that he was against the plans for coexistence with his bank.
Regardless of that it seems to be clearer that the union of the different banks in the field of public law is necessary.
Well, when the Bavarian parliamentary elections are going to pass, BayernLB's union with Baden-Württemberg regional bank could make progress.
For Helaba, that’s not necessarily good news.
If the pressure continues to merge will increase, Helaba will lack the partners to do that.
In the south the bank could be just a young partner, although so far it emerged much better from the financial crisis than the buildings of Stuttgart and Munich.
On the other hand the Sparkassen - und Giroverband of Hesse-Turingia, which owns 85 percent of Helaba, at the beginning of the year avoided coexistence plans with the West LB.
In any case, only the Nord LB remains.
But such geostrategic reflections are only one part.
On the other hand it is the compatibility of different banking models.
In June Merl asked a fundamental question about a business model that could guarantee the future for regional banks, that the deutsche Sparkassen- und Giro- Verband until now gave no answer.
Ultimately you can decompose the West LB, but that, of course, isn’t the bank’s own desire.
Thus, also in the letter of the board of directors of the bank it is said that it would try to find a complete solution for the entire bank
As you can combine the coexistence between unique parts of the bank with the DEKA, that will show time.
Oktoberfest's second weekend is known as "The Italian Weekend"
For Elena it's the first time for Luca already the third or fourth.
But this time, he's assisted by Elena as his girlfriend, and that's why everything seems different, he says.
Behind them, next to a 5-liter barrel of beer Kaiser is built a huge bear tiger that shows nearly 200 Oktoberfest participants that low sounds he knows how to produce in his throat.
First Elena gives Luca a slap, then a kiss.
They came to Verona from Bologna.
From there, from the car park next to Porta Nuova train station, tonight at 23:45 three buses leave, ` towards Munich, the beer party', foreseeable arrival at 6:30 in the morning.
Three buses are planned mainly for the Italians, a bus is only for Brazilians.
In one of the corners of the car park next to its flag are singing the South Americans, they had already begun to celebrate at night.
With a lot of noise, says Marco Guarda, which is nothing for the Italians.
Marco, who wears a long coat with an artificial fur lining and glasses with silver-colored temples, belongs to these buses.
For five years they come to the Oktoberfest, taking into account that there are only three excursions this year.
At night along the way there, during the day in the meadow, at 22.30 the return.
Spending the night there means only unnecessary expenses, Marco says.
The trip costs 75 euros, including the welcome reception with a Kaiser beer that was made according to the Bavarian Purity law, sickness insurance and the German-Mark guide attended a language course in Frankfurt.
At night the buses are already on the road on the highway with the "Brennero" direction
There's no beer, not yet.
Quietly reign on the bus, travellers are sleeping.
It's okay like that, they'll still need the forces.
He stops at Brixen and Holzkirchen, where other buses with the Italian license plate make another break on Highway 8 shortly before Munich.
Finally, when Marco’s group has the planned arrival at 6.30 a.m. in the car park next to Prado de Teresa, there are already 50 other buses from all over Europe.
Elena, Luca and the others meet, Marco has his last speech on how to proceed.
First, put on a yellow hat.
There, on the left, "Oktoberfest" is written, next door in gothic lyrics is the page of Marco's travel office on the internet: "conoscersiviaggiando.it".
Second: "When the doors of the tent are opened, that means marching!" shouts Marco in the early morning.
"March!" March and occupy the back sites in the tent.
"Don't take the places ahead, because we're going to block, and we're all with yellow caps don't sit on the same bench, spread out all the way!"
A liter of beer, roars Marco, costs 8.25 euros.
Don't forget the tip
Show the security people that we have a good tone!
He barely gets out of his place, he'll be busy now!"
Thirdly: "This afternoon at exactly ten thirty you have to arrive here!" Have you understood?
And now everyone's going to Oktoberfest.
One, to mark the way, tie the yellow caps in the trees, traffic signs and even in a poster of the elections of a large People’s Party of Bavaria.
You want to be able to recognize the way back.
It’s Oktoberfest’s second weekend that’s known as “The Italian Weekend”
There is no exact data on the number of people; these are 50,000 people who make the trip over the Alps and stormingly enter tents, 10 percent of all came especially this weekend from Italy.
The Munich police receive help from seven policemen from the Autonomous Province of Bolzano, Italian volunteers help the Bavarian Red Cross who makes a statistic of the nations present, where the Italians, with more than 200 medical assistance, in front of the English (about 60 assists) and the Austrians occupy the first place.
The Italians' favorite tent is so called Hofbräuzelt.
Sleepless Nights for Hypo Real Estate Creditors
Germany’s banking system is relatively stable, Federal Finance Minister Peter Steinbrück said last week.
How well, that the politician used the word "relatively" and added that the German banking field will also be affected by critical trends.
This has happened after the weekend.
Hypo Real Estate (HRE), Munich’s real estate financier, which is listed on the DAX index, receives from a consortium of German banks a one-billion-dollar loan to resist market turbulence.
On Monday a person who knows the situation very well told Reuters: credit aid amounted to 35 billion euros.
The share of capital that the Hypo Real Estate is going to use has to throw interest.
Money comes as from the private banks also from those of public law.
The reason for that is the losses of subsidiary Depfa.
According to a report, state financiers with the money that was borrowed for long-term projects were financed just a short period of time – which now, due to distrust in the markets, is no more possible.
In the first half of the year the bank’s capital reserve in cash has fallen by 95 percent, 2.37 million euros, also the share of equity fell slightly from 1.6 percent to 1.45 percent.
Compared to the same period last year’s continued income from financial investments and net profits of financial operations fell to zero, indicting revenues for debtors, and some securities also from the dissolution of credit business provisions tended to fall by more than 70 percent, by 5 million euro.
Only thanks to the high and high revenues from reimbursements of compensation expenses from the restructuring of the former Depfa group as well as interest reimbursement under the federal tax code and businesses organized for consortium companies, the negative balance could accuse a deficit with approximately 16 percent more.
After its privatization in 1990 the former state financier was initially lost in speculations with industrial credits for the properties, which served as a reason for the foundation of the Aareal bank.
Since you couldn’t make a lot of money from the financing of state projects, the Defa began to engage intensively on projects in the field of infrastructure and the financing of community projects by private and as well as state (Private-Public-Partnership PPP).
Now the Hypo Real Estate has to make amortizations about the value of the subsidiary that will have an "essential material effect" on the group's consolidated profit and loss account, it is said very inaccurately.
It's a fact they've canceled the dividends.
By 2007 they were canceled to two-thirds.
After the acquisition of Depfa the Hypo Real Estate became a major state and financial financier in the field of infrastructure.
As the bank does not own the customer deposits, he, compared to other banks, turns out to be more dependent on refinancing in the interbank market.
With U.S. investment bank Lehman Brothers, what happened two weeks agount, granting interbank loans fell essentially because banks were saving their liquidity.
Each year the Hypo Real Estate needs almost 50 billion euros to finance a portion of Defa’s credit portfolios of its short-term refinancing measures.
According to the Hypo Real Estate report, the bank covers with a credit the need for the group’s financing for a short time and the company is assured of “the influencement of the international money markets that are now essentially unfit to function”
Other sources say that thanks to this money refinancing is guaranteed until the end of 2009.
Georg Funke, chairman of the board of directors of the Hypo Real Estate, explained that the Hypo Real Estate Group would not need money markets for the foreseeable time.
The German central bank and the Federal Financial Services Surveillance Institute (BaFin) are on the basis that the competitiveness of the Hypo Real Estate Group from now on is assured.
That’s what shareholders and creditors have to expect from the bank.
But because of the dynamics and imponderability of the crisis there is no record.
It is even imaginable that you do not have to need funding in its full volume.
However, the opposite cannot be excluded.
There was a voice that on the last hour of Sunday the bank was still almost insolvency, so temporary salvation also cannot reassure at least worried people.
The share price fell to 75 percent, 3.30 euros.
Borrowing courses, on the contrary, are really good.
While priority debts almost don’t change, borrowing courses based on the position on the property registry tend clearly downward.
Affected are above all the loans of the former subsidiary Württemberg Hypo and with the reason the loans whose expirations exceed 2009.
After the remarkable growth of the banking crisis and acquisition of Depfa that affected the Hypo Real Estate, the current value of its borrowings that were previously an investment for speculation must be considered as dependent on the stability of the international financial system.
As long as emitting banks, governments and banks that are little affected are still ready to support the system, in the meantime you can start from pension depreciation within term.
Or something’s going to happen, which nobody risks imagining – the financial crisis is going to overcome in the next 15 months.
But seeing cross-news about partial statization, now the security that is already at its limit became a justified hope.
That’s going to be a reason, because creditors will spend the sleepless nights, smashing your head over the decision about their isolation of enthusiasm.
Still short-term investors can put the end and use transportation on a new account of losses for upcoming benefit compensation tax payments on the change in the future.
Sylvana and the Secrets of Bent?-Box
When the first day Sylvana Hiltrop, a 16-year-old girl, had to perform at Tachibana Highschool the girls began to laugh: The German is totally "kawaii"!
What does that mean?
Sylvana knows the word of Mangas - in a report on the exchanges she recounts Japan.
"The first day at a school in Japan.
I felt nervous.
Before I went to school, I was afraid.
I live on the edge of Tokyo in the Kawasaki direction and go by train 40 minutes to Tachibana Highschool.
Alone I had to find my way, luckily I didn't get lost.
It seems that the beginning of the classes will not be fixed as rigorously as in my house in Lower Saxony.
From eight in the morning the students come, at nine minus twenty begins a small meeting with the teachers, the 'home room'.
Before the class began, I had come to introduce myself.
In addition, I am not a person who speaks gladly in the audience, especially before a class of 40 students.
As they still have the school uniform I wore an old skirt from the mother of my host family and also a blouse, blue socks and black leather shoes.
Well, so dressed I got to the pulpit and tried to pronounce everything correctly: "Sayonara Wo she Sylvana..." - my name is Sylvana, I'm from Germany and in a week it will be my birthday.
At the moment I was very happy because for two years I had started studying this language.
All 31 girls in the class have whispered, laughed and beckoned and all the time I've heard the word "kawaii"
I've known her about my sleeves.
That belongs to the survival vocabulary of Japanese girls and means "mona, cute"
Then I slipped quickly into my place.
The girl next door had a big smile, for her it was an honor that the exchange girl had to sit beside her.
The rest of the class was pretty quiet, but when the gong sounded, I really felt assaulted.
Everyone spoke at the same time, laughed and asked many questions - at the same time it is very difficult to understand Japanese English.
Then at recess everyone took out their Bentos.
The mother of my host family also made a Lanchbox for me - it's something other than boring pieces of German bread.
It had rice with herbs, small sausages, cucumber salad and algae, fruit and something like tofu meat.
In most cases I have no idea what like here in Japan.
Things are rare and have a new taste.
What's for sure is that everything's very rich.
Well, perhaps with the exception of marinated plums in salt, bufff!
In Japanese schools, bentos are not just a lunch.
Sometimes it happens that a girl prepares a bento made in very artistic mode for a boy and gives it to him in hope of being able to get to know him better during a recess.
That's what I read about at my Manga-Comics.
I'm really curious to see if I can see it here too.
"Why precisely Japan?" my friends asked me when I told them I wanted to go to Tokyo to attend a year's school.
Then he always replied:
"Well, 'cause it fascinates me."
I've been trying to read Mangas for years.
In order to better understand comics and culture, one day I began to study some Japanese.
For me it was absolutely certain that one day I will travel there.
Also because I have a skinny by tradition and customs.
Here they have great value.
On the one hand, Japan is a country of the latest technologies and trends, on the other hand it is a severe, disciplined and traditional country.
As it’s all well organized, I still didn’t feel lost here although Tokyo is the biggest city I’ve ever seen in my life.”
Rats also have feelings
It is said that a rat or cockroach feeling the danger flees, why is it also afraid?
Joseph Le Doux, the scientist in the field of neurology is convinced that many animals also have feelings.
How can you control if they, behaving in the manner similar to us, feel the same?
Contributions from famous scientists have been published in an internet magazine called "Edge" for many years.
SPIEGEL ONLINE presents in a series the chosen answers to the question What do you think what is true without being able to prove it?
I believe that animals have sensations and other states of consciousness without me or anyone else being able to prove it until now, although we can’t even prove that other people have consciousness.
But in this case at least we can expect it because all human brains have the same fundamental configuration.
But as soon as we dedicate ourselves to other species and include questions about sensation and in general about consciousness, we enter into the unfamiliar realm because the hardware doesn’t coincide.
When a rat finds itself in danger, it does the same as the other animals: the dead man becomes, flees or attacks.
People behave in a similar way, from which some scientists make conclusions about comparable subjective experience.
Naturally I don’t think so.
Two aspects of the brain structure make it difficult to spread our subjective experience to that of animals.
Firstly, they almost always include the circuits associated by human consciousness of the lateral prefrontal lobe of the cerebral cortex (because of their involvement in short memory and the executive functions that direct behavior).
This wide part is much more developed in the case of people than that of the other primates and it seems that it is absolutely lacking in other creatures.
Considering at least the aspects related to our consciousness that depends on the prefrontal lobe of the cerebral cortex, including knowledge about who we are and the ability to glide and decide, there is a reason to suppose that even man differs from the other primates.
Another peculiarity is found in the linguistic nature of man: Since the majority of his experience is united with the tongue, that often means that consciousness depends on it.
In this case the animals can be excluded.
But even though consciousness would not depend on the language, it would influence it so that the consciousness of the animals, created however, in many cases would be differentiated from most of our states of consciousness.
That’s why it’s hard to explain how the consciousness of other animals works.
If that, as something interesting and subjective, is not allowed to measure because it has the special hardware, nor allowed to be analyzed through our experiences, so its research presents great problems.
Most of my interventions refer to the content of consentious experience, but at the same time there is also another aspect of consciousness that would have to be easier for scientific research.
We could investigate the processes of animal consciousness without taking into account their contents, and that is what happens during primate short memory studies, especially in the example of visualization.
But with this approach followed by Christof Koch and Francis Crick the essential happens rather to the neutral correlates of consciousness than to the causal mechanisms: The two may or may not be similar.
Curiously this approach highlights the importance of the prefrontal lobe of the cerebral cortex for the formation of visualization.
And what does it turn out for sensations?
I owe to the fact that in the emotional system a part of the brain is activated that is responsible for it, the same thing that happens with fear.
What we describe as fear is therefore a state of mind that we are in when the activity of the brain occupies a space of the defense system (or its consequences such as the reactions of the body).
Seen from this point of view the sensations are very fixed to part of the cerebral cortex which distinguishes primates and above all man.
From the point of view of the linguistic nature they follow classifications of fine feelings because we can differentiate and classify the states with the help of words and grammar in order to be able to describe the states of others by ourselves.
For example Antonio Damascus, on the contrary, thinks that the sensations derive from the simple activities of the parts of the cerebral cortex responsible for the bodily feelings and the brain stem, the same Jaak Pankseep thinks, but he concentrates more on the brain stem.
As this network hasn’t changed much during human evolution, you can absolutely refer to different types and their sensations.
For theoretical reasons I can't go against that, but I consider it not likely.
Pakseep argues that what rats and men feel as fear, possibly that feels in two cases as well: But how can you control whether rats and men behaving similarly feel the same?
Seeing the danger a cockroach flees, because he's scared?
I am of the opinion that the likeness of behavior still does not prove the likeness of experience.
That’s true that neuronal comparison helps: rats and men have similar brain trunks, cockroaches on the contrary don’t have at least one brain.
Is the brain's trunk that's responsible for sensations?
Even if it is possible to test it for men: How can it be tested in the case of rats?
I think that rats and other mammals, possibly also cockroaches (who knows?), have sensations.
But I don’t know how you can prove it.
I’d rather investigate emotional behavior from rats than emotional sensations because their sensations are supposedly fundamentally distinguished from us (because human consciousness refers to special circuits and the tongue).
In any case, progress in the field of neurology is expected here as long as the same of rats and men is measured.
Since I don’t investigate the language and consciousness of rats, as well as sensations, I don’t know if they exist.
It can be said that I don’t see beyond my nose, but I’d rather move forward than to work permanently without results.
Well, I'm a practical emotionalist.
