“We need more of the feeling and the dribbling,” Jol demands.
After the Voting Defeat
Fear is spreading on Wall Street.
The first news about the failure of the banks’ salvation package dropped the Down Jones a certain period to 700 points.
That was the loss of the biggest points during a day in its history.
Then the Dow Jones recovered a bit.
Around 20:30 one of the world’s largest stock market barometers priced a 5 percent deficit at 10,579 units.
