The time has come in which no morality exists anymore: we can mistreat, torture, arbitrarily imprison a Canadian citizen as the so far minority head of government wants (what will happen after October 14?).
Many voters believe that they will find salvation in a party that commends Virtue, Law and Order: they do not see that this government renounced what made the reputation and dignity of our country.
Mr. Toews the shame is caused by this resignation and by nothing else.
Free Opinion - Barrick Gold's Orwellian Speech
In its Sept. 17 issue, Le Devoir issued a letter from Mr. Patrick J. Garver, vice president and director of Canadian miner Barrick Gold.
Following an Orwellian logic, Barrick Gold claims that the world’s largest gold company attempted a six-million-euro defamation process against three authors and a small publishing house in order to spark a “transparent public debate.”
If it is true that the judges are independent and impartial, it is not the truth they judge, especially in the case of defamation persecutions, but the law.
Unsurprisingly, this fundamental difference is completely concealed by Mr. Garver.
Why, according to Barrick Gold, the best way to conduct a public debate would be to harm whoever dares to hold a position contrary to his?
The result of the lawsuit is of little importance, the authors and editor of the book Noir Canada must spend considerable sums in order to prepare his defense and fight, with very unequal weapons, against an army of lawyers sustained by the mine’s almost bottomless pockets.
Tactic, in these unequal struggles, is often to ruin the defendants in order to impose an amicable settlement that the opposition will muzzle in addition to frightening whoever will dare to re-examine the issue.
If Barrick Gold had truly wanted a public debate, it is in front of public opinion that he would have had to present his view of the facts.
Contrary to what is done in several countries where Barrick Gold works, debates in Canada are usually done by changing ideas and not slugging.
It sufficed therefore that the miner opened her books, her files and established a real debate, through the newspapers, the media, the publications and the financing of independent search teams that would have been able to clarify the issue.
But Barrick Gold doesn’t seem to rely on public opinion and he rejects petitions and support letters for Noir Canada’s authors.
Possibly Mr. Garver could explain how you can ask for a "public" debate despising his views?
According to the vice president, it seems that this word designates only high-paid lawyers and not for all Canadians; that represents a very limited view of the concept.
In democracy, detractors also have the right to speak.
What doesn’t understand – or what Barrick Gold doesn’t want to understand – is that the public holding the authors and editors of Noir Canada does it primarily because it rejects the mining company’s brutal way.
This public is willing to listen to Barrick and to judge him, but based on civilized changes of arguments, and not within the framework of what many people perceive as a persecution-gag (chasing the "public debate", Barrick Gold has just placed a request with respect to the authors of Noir Canada intimating them not to use this word anymore).
In addition to Mr. Garver’s surreal discourse, Barrick Gold’s process is a direct attack on the freedom of university search and truth, essential to all democratic societies.
Denies the right to cite credible sources and make a debate on facts and interpretations, which represent the basis of intellectual work.
If it is impossible to study and argue about subjects who displease the rich companies of this world in a country like Canada, under penalty of many persecutions, who can do it?
If Barrick Gold truly wanted public and transparent debate, he could do so by following the scientific standards used by the authors of Noir Canada.
He has a right of reply.
The university world, to which we belong, has long known how to manage debates and disagreements and resolve conflicts.
Barrick Gold’s inordinate persecution clearly shows that, contrary to what he intends, he doesn’t look forward to a transparent debate.
It’s a loss for the university world, but also for public debate in Canada, and it’s time for governments to place devices that limit this kind of abusive persecution.
Wall Street bailout operation – Democrats and Republicans agree
The Bush administration and congressional leaders, both Republicans and Democrats, finally reached an agreement yesterday on the most important economic rescue plan since the Great Depression of the 30’s.
The new version of the 700 billion U.S. dollar plan that aims to curb the financial crisis that has rocked Wall Street for months has yet to be confirmed by both Chambers of Congress.
It foresees in particular: a better control on the part of those elected of their implementation, of new mechanisms that aim to ensure the reimbursement of the public money invested, of the new provisions to contain the number of intoxicated houses the non-payment, as well as a right of control over the salaries paid to the leaders of the rescued companies.
U.S. Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson, House Speaker Nancy Pelosi and Republican Representative at the Negotiating Bureau, Senator Judd Gregg, announced the good news a few minutes after midnight yesterday at the end of a two-day negotiation marathon.
“We made great strides with a view to an agreement that will be effective in the markets,” said Bush administration representative Henry Paulson.
“Everything has been done to cover the economy and ordinary Americans in the face of the current crisis on Wall Street,” she said.
“It’s the fundamental point: if we don’t do this, the trauma, chaos, and disturbances about Americans’ daily lives will be immense,” said Republican Judd Gregg.
The negotiations had run out very quickly in recent hours because they feared the effect it would bring about a new failure in the mood of investors.
The last hour they had set was the opening of the markets this morning.
The two candidates in the U.S
Democratic Senator Barack Obama was given certain provisions to reach the agreement, particularly that which would allow owners to keep their domicile and over the salary of state-surviving business leaders.
" When taxpayers are asked to take extraordinary measures because of the irresponsibility of some, we must not congratulate themselves.
But these measures are necessary," he said on American television.
His Republican adversary, John McCain, interrogated in another network to know if he would vote for the proposed plan, replied: “I’d like to see the details, but I’m looking forward to voting for it.”
" The important points I read [show] that it is something that we will have to digest and with which we will be able to anticipate.
He said that the option to do nothing is not acceptable."
The 700 billion plan aims to buy doubtful debts, risky and invendible assets from American financial institutions with taxpayers’ money.
It comes after 14 months of a crisis caused by the outbreak of a real estate bubble that first led to the collapse of risky mortgage loans before spreading to other more common forms of credit securities (PCAAs) and provoking a liquidity freeze and a disbandment of banks and financial institutions.
It’s a group of elected Republicans that had changed the first draft deal last week.
We believe we’ve come out of stagnation since the Democrats accepted that certain “toxic” assets of companies in difficulty are only insured by the government, rather than bought.
With the aim of bringing roughness for everyone in Congress, we also added a provision stipulating that if the government had to bear losses for five years with this program, it could impose new rates that would want to help it recover money.
The new plan envisages the payment of a first part of 250 billion to which 100 billion can be added if it seems necessary to the president.
The payment of another 350 billion would have to be confirmed by another vote from Congress.
Instead of his help, Washington will get stakes in the relief companies that will earn him dividends in the event of profits and that he will be able to sell again when the storm will be passed.
The federal government will have the possibility of delaying the procedures of embargoes that concerned housing obtained with real estate loans according to this plan, as well as setting limits on remuneration and cash compensation paid to the leaders of companies affected by the crisis.
The architects of the plan would like to see him put to the vote of the House of Representatives from today and that of the Senate next Wednesday.
Despite all your efforts, you’re still unsure that your plan will be approved.
Some people continued to protest this project yesterday, both Republicans and Democrats.
Republican Scott Garrett, a member of the House finance commission, told his constituents that "with all the evidence, Washington doesn't want to understand."
"We have a very serious financial problem.
There are solutions.
But it’s not what it’s about taking advantage of taxpayers.”
Rep. Brad Sherman, who is an animator of a small group in Congress, presents the problems differently, but comes to the same conclusion.
"Four hundred professors of economics, among whom three Nobel laureates, wrote us to tell us: we asked Congress not to rush and carefully examine the path that must be taken," he declared yesterday.
At this very moment, in Europe, we again had proof of the global nature of the crisis.
After an urgent meeting, the three Benelux countries announced the partial nationalization of the Fortis banking group for 11.2 billion euros (16.3 billion dollars).
Intervention by the governments of Belgium, the Netherlands and Luxembourg had been necessary after the French bank BNP Paribas announced that it renounced to buy its bankrupt competitor since it lost 2 billion euros (2.9 billion dollars) during the crisis of risky real estate loans in the United States.
Fortis employs 85 000 people and is part of the twenty largest European banks and the ten largest insurers.
" This is not money lost," Dutch Finance Minister Wouter Bos said yesterday.
Instead, we regain a voting right in the bank and influence.
It’s precisely something that savers and families will now appreciate that times are uncertain.”
During this time, on the other side of La Mancha, the British government seemed to want to nationalize another bank suffering from the financial crisis.
According to the English press, the government would take care of all outstanding loans at Bradford and Bringley and more than 41 billion euros (75.5 billion dollars) of real estate loans.
The Spanish bank Santander announced yesterday that it is the one that would buy the branches and bank accounts of the British bank.
Bradford and Bringley would be the second bank, after Northern Rock, that the British government would have to nationalize from the beginning of this financial crisis.
Paul Newman (1925-2008) - Death of a Compromised Icon
His blue eyes represented his triumph for so long.
Had the American actor with a lovely smile liberated from his narcissistic side?
Yes and no.
His modesty, his sensibility and a talent that was evident will also have distanced him from the register of power that the true sacred monsters have.
But what a great corridor in the background!
Paul Newman, who died on Friday at the age of 83, from lung cancer on his Connecticut ranch, remains one of the last U.S. film icons of the fast years.
It is less phenomenal than Brando, whom he looked very much like and who was long regarded as a rival in the cinema, more prudent in his game, certainly more fragile, but also an apostle of freedom and the outbreak of dramatic covenants.
Mixed bloods often make magnificent children.
He was born in Ohio in 1925 to a German Jewish father and a mother of Hungarian origin.
One of the glorious faces of the American dream will be born from these European roots.
Without excessive ego, the ultimate brand of quality.
Because in it was projected an entire country in love with self-made man, of the fighter of the Pacific war, wounded in combat, who at the beginning of the 1950s studied dramatic art in Yale, then frequented the Actor's Studio of New York, before succeeding in the theater, on television and soon in the cinema.
This man who served for civil rights was also the car driver who qualified in second place in the 24 hours of Le Mans in 1979, dubbed by a sex symbol, albeit a member of a model couple formed since 1958 with actress Joanne Woodward.
Also disappear with him the secret sides of this secret, discreet and committed star, allergic to the scandals of show business that we do not know very well.
He is an honest man in the noblest sense of the word.
Paul Newman’s death sparked vertigous moviegoers this weekend, while his great black-screened roles from memories are tackled.
More than a half-century of the 7th American art in perpetual moving parades through it.
Many memories come back to memory such as Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid's (1969), the young man who rejects his sensual wife (with Elizabeth Taylor) in La Gata over Tennessee Williams adapted zinc roof in 1958.
Closer to us (1990), we evoked his sensitive Mr. Bridge, disturbed by a marriage that didn’t fulfill all his promises.
Others like Paul Newman have gone down in the history of cinema.
Robert Wise’s boxer Rocky Graziano, a criminal, tormented, violent in Robert Wise’s Somebody Up Up There Likes Me, a role intended for James Dean, repeated after his death, who truly launched Newman in 1956.
This nice mangante in the sumptuous film The Sting, Oscar for Best Picture in 1973.
A bitter and avenging billiard player in Robert Rossen's magnificent film The Hustler (1961), he will reprise Martin Scorsese's The Color of Money, which earned him his only nine-nomination Oscar in 1987.
This face that changes over the years, it was him.
Still he.
Times change during his career.
Young people know him mainly thanks to Slap Shot of George Roy Hill (1977), in Reggie Dunlop, coach of an unorthodox ice hockey team.
His fans re-watched him in 1994 on The Hudsucker Proxy of the Coen brothers.
With a last role as godfather of the Irish Maffia at Sam Mendes Road to Perdition in 2003, the curl was curled.
Contrary to several film legends who abandoned the race quite soon, Newman stayed a lot in the world of cinema, denouncing Hollywood, its golds, its fasticoes and its concessions.
French filmmaker Bertrand Tavernier considered it, with humor, "as a challenge that lives in "underplaying" and that judges its benefits too supported.
The profession wasn’t always easy for the beautiful Paul Newman to whom the papers arrived for a long time doing nothing.
However, he played less often the role of a young gallant than of marginal: neurotics, alcoholics, bastards or desperate, whose traits reflected the rebellions.
As a filmmaker, Newman revealed sides his unwell-known true pudic sensibility.
His film Raquel, Raquel, in 1968 (according to Canada's novel Margaret Laurence), with his wife Joanne Woodward in the lead role, described a female portrait of melancholy.
He who lost his son Scott because of an overdose dedicated his film Harry and Son in 1984, a work of modesty and sadness.
“Among the numerous tributes that were unleashed yesterday for Newman, his great friend and former comrade Robert Redford (had worked together at The Sting and Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid) he said, deeply saddened: ‘my life and my country were better thanks to their existence’
Generosity, love of existence are important traits of the deceased actor.
On the other side of his legendary career, there is also a great activist for civil rights, ecology, independent cinema, an accountant against the excesses of Hollywood.
We will have seen a lot of his face reigning over the bottles of vinaigrette sauce, sauces, cookies and other foods, judging this method as a method of bad taste, although he started out as a gag.
The benefits of these sales were given to their Childhood Foundation in difficulty.
Newman, rather than content himself with his myth, will have committed himself to the end.
He left his five daughters a letter containing these phrases: " always and to the end, your father was incredibly grateful for his good star.
It was a privilege to be there.”
And a privilege for us to have followed the career of an American artist so lucid and so generous.
In short, a model citizen.
What did they produce at the Zuschlag &amp; Co. invoice factory?
Very soon, on October 8, criminal proceedings will begin against János Zuschlag and his accomplices.
The politician and his accomplices are accused of committing frauds of significant damage, by way of business, continuously and in an organized manner in addition to other crimes, including falsifying documents.
According to the Public Prosecutor's Office, they used the funds obtained in the public competitions for their own purposes, justifying on many occasions the fulfillment of the tasks with false invoices.
The public funds and that of the municipalities - in its entirety about 65 million HUF - stopped in part in the treasury of the Fiatal Baloldal organization and partly in the pocket of individuals.
The method, which was also released by the researchers, was to justify the collection of the funds obtained in public tenders with false invoices behind which there was no real execution, the different associations never fulfilled their assumed obligations.
According to the indictment, most of the bills were false.
For this they obtained the checkbooks in the market of the Józsefváros District and the circular seals were manufactured in the city of Kiskunhalas.
And the question that on behalf of which company the forged bill was to be carried out was decided among others on that tour of the Upper Region of the Balaton where János Zuschlag sent to István Lados.
The latter confessed that for this purpose he had to choose hostels and restaurants.
He asked for invoices for their consumptions and these served as a model to make the invoices they presented among others in the competitions of the Ministry of Youth and Sports Affairs, in the Ministry of Social and Labor Affairs, as well as in the City Council of the Capital.
These invoices were signed mostly by István Lados and his accomplice András Őri, who according to our information rather wrote the reports necessary to obtain the public subsidies.
During one of his "study trips" Sides chose a brewery.
According to two bills issued in 2003 by Zuschlag and his accomplices, this gastronomic center provided food for a group of ninety people from the Biztos Pont Egyesület Association.
However - according to the manager of the center - so many people don't fit at the same time in that place.
Likewise, the bill issued in the summer of 2002 for the Jobb JövőÉrt Foundation - later called Együtt a Harmadik Évezredért - was full of formal and contextual errors.
Well, a hostel in the town of Badacsonytomaj had only three rooms and more than ten people could not stay there in one night, however in the bill consisted of one hundred and thirty people.
But the manufacturers of great fantasy invoice also exaggerated when pointed out to the gastronomic center Pigal Kft. because in the holding of books of the same - according to the information given to the Prosecutor's Office - there were no documents on behalf of Jobb Jövőért and Hoppá.
Győző Farkas, the company’s manager, informed hvg.hu that when he was summoned by the prosecutor’s office and was shown the bills, he already knew that these were false documents.
"On the seal the name of our company and the NIF appeared in the wrong place."
He added: in addition to formal problems it did not agree that according to the bill, one hundred people were accommodated, since they have only eleven rooms in which there are not so many people.
In addition, the bill also included meals, while the restaurant hasn't worked for a long time.
Enthusiastic invoice manufacturers were also not informed that the travel agency chosen in Budapest exclusively organizes trips abroad, souch that in the cash payment bill they foolishly indicated as a service a trip within Hungary, which also did not coincide with the agency’s billing practice.
In addition - as was known during the investigation ‐ they also included VAT in the document, despite the fact that travel outside the territory of the European Union was exempt from taxes.
Among other things the VAT measure was also incorrect in the four documents issued by the Hotel Révfülöp Kft. for the Jobb Jövőért foundation, since the services of that company are not loaded with 25 but only with 15 percent VAT, in addition the employees of the hotel only extended invoices made by machine however the invoice was manual.
In addition, the "shippers" made other mistakes as well, as in the case of a company in which they put on the bill as an activity carried out the road transport to which - it was known during the investigations of the prosecutor's office - does not carry out the company founded as an investment consultant.
Also due to formal differences - inadequate format of the invoice, false stamp - it was known that the invoices issued for Együtt to Harmadik Évezredért Alapítvány, for XXI. Századi Kulturális Egyesület and for Biztos Pont.
As in the case of Ravenna Bt. or Kunfehértó Sports Camp, whose representatives denied having issued those bills.
The counterfeiters also also paid attention that when Fiatal Városért Egyesület’s group ate there (2001) Nyíregyháza’s HIB Kft was in the process of liquidation, that is why the person in charge of the liquidation process – according to our information – denied having issued such a document.
They consciously issued the bills
Another group of manufacturers of fake invoices are made up of those who were aware that they should issue fictitious invoices.
The Esély Budapestért Alapítvány Foundation, at the request of Fiatal Baloldal - Ifjú Szocialisták, issued an invoice worth some four million HUF on behalf of the Együtt Foundation to Harmadik Évezredért.
The manager of the Collab Kft. - according to the indictment - was persuaded by one of the defendants, Ludovic Györfi, to issue fictitious bills.
It also collaborated with Zuschlag and its accomplices the Biogate Kft., currently under liquidation process, which in 2003 supplied invoices worth approximately five million HUF to the Jobb Jövőért Alapítvány foundation, the association Atlasz Egyesület and the Vörösfenyő Egyes�ület association
There was no movement of capital either, because then they canceled the prepared invoices but they forgot to record in their documents this entity.
The next group of fake invoice manufacturers includes those who have some connection with the defendants.
For example Ivan Kubatov was the surge of the Ukrainian manager of Delta Trio SL with fictitious headquarters in Budapest, which dealt with the trade of fuels and vehicles.
This company issued numerous invoices worth approximately HUF in the months of October, November and December 2005 on the sale of computer media.
According to the data of the investigation these invoices were bought by the Cash Investment Kft. of Kiskunhalas, which since September 14, 2005 is under liquidation process.
The manager of this company was a Romanian whom Ivan Kubatov should have also dispatched documents related to the company between 2002 and 2005.
We have information that Kubatov acknowledged during the investigation that he issued on behalf of the company invoices for the Atlasz, for Hoppá and for Együtt to Harmadik Évezredért Alapítvány charging the amount himself.
The Fa-Bani Jos Faipari Kft. and the Jos-Investment Bt. were founded by Romanian masons at the express request of Ivan Kubatov.
However, none of the companies worked effectively because - according to the defendant - that they did not receive work.
But he took advantage of these companies, since at the request of his accomplice the lawyer Zsolt Szente, who prepared the registration documents of the company, issued invoices on behalf of the companies for the organizations linked to Zuschlag: for the Atlasz and for the Y-Generáció.
Kubatov on behalf of the Cash Investment, the Delta Trió, the Fa-Bani Jos, the Jos Investment and the Linaxtrade gave a total of 15 invoices to different entities worth 14.2 million HUF.
The Public Prosecutor's Office considered that Kubatov received the VAT and 10% of the amount of the invoices.
That man even took advantage of Szi-Beri's company to issue fictitious invoices used in the Biztos Pont contest.
The Y-Generáció and Szövetség to Modern Magyarországért presented a contest in January 2006 to Táncsics Mihály Alapítvány (TMA), public utility entity of the Socialist Party.
From the contest they obtained 500 thousand HUF respectively, but did not use the money for the objectives of the contest.
In order for this not to be discovered, they submitted to the TMA five fictional invoices received from the Works Team Kft.
These were the invoices found during the registration of the office that Árpád Kemecsei had at the headquarters of the Ministry of Education.
Part of the defendants will likely recount in the trial - as they did in the Prosecutor's Office - the course of falsifying the bills.
Most interestible may be the confession of the chief defendant János Zuschlag himself, if he decides to dismantle everything.
For his confessions so far have not been very detailed and although he repeatedly promised to talk about everything, this he has not done until the present.
The question is: what interest does he have?, because perhaps in exchange for the return of most of the money - fifty million HUF - the socialists reached an agreement with him so that Zusi assumes all the responsibilities.
Who, on the other hand, for these days could even be offended, since in order to alleviate his prison conditions he requested house arrest, but it was repeatedly denied him.
While the numerous perpetrators of economic crimes of much higher value, who never returned the money, walk freely or at least can wait in their own home for the sentence, he has no chance for that.
Overlapping Psychology: Why Do We Spend More Money?
Auction participants are prone to spending more money and overestimating the product.
Neurologists and economists at New York University uncovered the neurological-economic foundations of this known and seemingly irrational behavior.
According to the study published in the journal Science, people don’t want to lose in competencies such as eBay auctions, which is why they prefer to pay even an excessive price.
The scientists tried to establish the neurological scheme of this "game" by means of experimental auctions.
One of the volunteer groups played lottery, the other participated in an auction and in the meantime it was examined using the functional magnetic resonance imaging system (fMRI) the active areas of the brain of the people participating in the experiment.
In both games the participants could win money, but during the auctions, where it is a fundamental element to bet more than the other, by losing the game the functioning of the complex called stratum located below the cerebral cortex was intensified.
This area of the brain, in addition to many other functions, plays a role in the "self prize" mechanism of the nervous system.
According to the scientists, the increase in bets is explained as a prevention so as not to provoke an intense reaction of the stratum.
To substantiate their theory, economists of the scientific group also conducted a financial follow-up study.
In this experiment three groups wagered against a person in different circumstances.
The control group was simply informed of the real value of the product in question, and its members gambled.
Another group in addition to this was promised that if they win, they would receive 15 dollars more prizes.
Instead, the third group received exactly 15 dollars before the auction, but in case of losing the auction the members of the group lost even that money.
Thus the only difference between the two groups was that for one the triumph was highlighted and for the other the failure.
However, by checking the neurologist hypothesis, members of the group playing "against failure" were willing to bet even more than the members of the control group and the "winning" group.
"These results cannot be deduced from any previously existing economic theory.
Well, those until now explained the phenomena of the auctions only with the joy of winning and with the prevention of risks.
Only visual neurological methods helped solve this contradiction between the two theories, so we now come up with a third explanation," said Andrew Schotter, a professor at New York University's faculty of economics.
Hepatitis: When should you go to your doctor?
In the world about five hundred million people suffer from chronic hepatitis B or C, and in Hungary chronic liver disease is considered one of the leading causes of death.
The number of people infected in this country is estimated at one hundred thousand, but only seven thousand receive treatment because many of the patients do not know that they are infected.
The denomination of hepatitis is the common name for different liver diseases caused by viruses.
The symptoms are very similar; liver infection and jaundice are characteristic, but their pathogens and the diseases caused are very different.
Hepatitis viruses in dependence on the pathogenic agent are spread through two main forms: hepatitis A and E by food (e.g. with water or infected food), hepatitis B, C, D and other viruses with blood and with body moods (sperm, vaginal mood, saliva).
It is advisable for travelers to protect themselves by vaccine against virus A and B, against C there are no vaccines.
Hepatitis A symptoms appear two to three weeks after consuming the infected food is manifested by a bad general condition, weakness, abdominal pain and nausea.
After this appears on the skin and white of the eyes the jaundice, the excrement becomes clear, dark-colored urine and healing can last even two - three weeks.
Annually, one million people die worldwide in cancer and cirrhosis from hepatitis B, the most serious forms of this disease.
The main reason for this is that according to the calculations, only one out of ten infected receives pharmacological treatment.
Hepatitis C can also have very serious consequences: without treatment it can lead to cirrhosis and even cancer.
Most those infected don’t know that they’re sick because this pathological agent gradually destroys liver cells and many times the first symptoms only appear 20-30 years later.
Prematural recognition, systematic medical monitoring is therefore very important.
It’s much more prevalent in three groups: people who had blood transfusion before 1991, drug users, and those with tattoos.
There are currently some 200 million people worldwide suffering from chronic hepatitis C.
As this disease can be discovered with a routine lab control as well, it is worth consulting with the doctor of the family when experiencing any unknown symptoms.
The disease is cured if discovered in time, it is possible to exterminate the virus of the organism, so it can suppress contagion and prevent cancer.
September 30 is World Hepatitis Day, which was first organized in 2004 by organizations representing the sick.
It aims to draw attention to the causes of chronic liver infections caused by viruses and the importance of their premature recognition.
Is it less painful for those who believe in God?
According to the result of a recent investigation, religious faith has a soothing effect that also relieved the death of the martyrs of Catholicism.
Scientists at the University of Oxford conducted an interesting experiment: they analyzed that religious belief in how it influences human pain - the British newspaper Telegraph reported.
In the framework of this singular experiment they applied electric shock to 12 Catholic believers and to the same amount of atheists, in the meantime everyone was looking at a painting of the Virgin Mary.
According to the results, Catholic believers were able to exclude most of their pain.
Thanks to the scanning technique of the human brain, it could be verified that Catholic believers were able to activate that part of their brain that is responsible for the regulation of pain.
This experiment is the first in the series of research in which among scholars also participate scientists, philosophers and theologians from the different departments of the University.
The analysis occurred as follows; they attached a sparkling instrument to the patient's left hand, which applied the electric shock.
The researchers asked the participants of the experiment to fix their gaze on two paintings; to the Virgin Mary, work of Sassoferrato of the 17th century and to Leonardo da Vinci’s 15th-century Arminy Lady.
Investigators were hopeful that the spectacle of the Virgin Mary would provoke a certain religious mood among the faithful, while choosing Leonardo’s oil because it was not too different from the other, and they thought it had reassuring effect.
Patients spent half an hour on an MRI scanner, receiving 20 electrical shocks in four successive parts while observing religious-themed painting or the other.
Catholics claimed that by looking at the Virgin Mary they felt in "security" as "protected", "reassured and in their heart peace reigned."
Looking at the religious-themed picture they felt 12 percent less pain than when they looked at Leonardo’s work.
The psychologist Miguel Farias who also participated in the experiment, thinks that with any such shocking image you can achieve a similar effect with atheists too, you just have to find the right image.
"We should find the portrait of a person they feel very positively for, as for a mother or a father," the psychologist said.
Anglican Bishop Tom Wright celebrated the outcome of the investigation.
"The exercise of faith should and in many cases really changes our personality," Wright added.
After these formidable results there is only one question: what effect would it have for the regulation of pain if the faithful were showned the Madonna of Leonardo or of another painter of his carving?
Would the vision of a high-quality Virgin Mary yield even better results?
You're what you say about yourself
On his 10th birthday Google can say: it can be found both in people’s pockets, and in the sky above their head; he knows where they spent their holidays, which doctors they visit, and what they care about.
But according to Eric Schmidt, one of the company’s executives, this is still not enough.
On the other hand the skeptics who make a parallel with the Orwelian vision do not see the essence of Web 2.0.
Eric Schmidt recently told the Financial Times that Google’s main objective is to gather as much personal data as possible about its users, and this is necessary to be able to meet the original objectives of Google’s founders: “Let’s gather in a system all the information in the world!”
According to the leader of Google, the company even after ten years of work that returned to the World is still in the initial phase of the effort to be able to treat all the information.
To the question that what is going to happen in five years Schmidt answered like this: I would like that Google could answer questions such as "What to do tomorrow?" or "What would be the job that would suit me best?" - however, the software will not be able to answer questions apparently so simple as long as there is not enough information from users.
Not all Internet users are aware that during their navigation on the Network, searched keywords, IP addresses and pages where they went at the end of the search are stored.
Thanks for example to Personalized Search that debuted two years ago, users can store their own browsing history, they can recheck what they were looking for before, what they opened and thanks to this history will generate much more personalized searches - in this same logic the Recommendations will be based, on which the system will offer us products and services based on the preferences previously defined and stored.
What will happen if they take advantage of my data against myself, if they collect information about my activities? - ask those users who worry about seeing Google’s informative monopoly.
In most cases rather the potential represented by the company is what may be fearful and not remorse, fear of punishment, longing for freedom or rebellion against power.
However, it is a fact already confirmed that they not only retain, but in justifiable cases also give third parties all the expressions sought, in these cases there is nothing that protects the personal rights of Internet users.
The most debated example of recent times was perhaps the coordinated action against Brazilian pedophiles, when Google gave the Brazilian government the information on its website, called Orkut, to identify pedophiles.
Instead, netizens who care about people’s rights, in the month of May were relieved when the company along with the EFF, an organization for the defense of electronic rights, successfully demonstrated in court that it was right in its litigation with the FBI: according to the sentence, Google cannot be forced, through any of the points of the constitution to supply any type of information secretly requested by the FBI.
(At the same time the federal government managed to achieve on the pretext of reinforcing the child protection law approved years ago, about fifty thousand Web addresses and about a thousand searched phrases, but without obtaining the search lists of individual users, nor the complete lists of websites and keywords of the last two months.)
This is quite contradictory the opinion about Google: it is criticized by those who are afraid to provide their personal data because they think that their privacy is harmed, their private life when they begin to use Google’s services, and rebel against it as against conservative multinational imaging companies.
Meanwhile, American geek culture and its enthusiastic followers, netizens and users from other countries, see in them the future generation, the "avant-garde corporation", not so to its rival, the Microsoft, cataloged by its Windows as conqueror of the World, no matter how much they both fight for the same goal.
This can happen because Google, unlike Microsoft, does not ask users for any identification code, or money for its applications, the code is open and the free program package, constantly updated and seems more youthful, more collaborative than the practice of the official software giant.
But it may also be because geeks see with precision the very problematic relationship between people’s rights and the Internet that occurred precisely by one of the most mentioned keywords in recent years: Web 2.0.
Web 2.0 is about collaboration, leaving intentional traces behind us and taking advantage of available communication channels, and while the measures of these varies individually, the essence remains the same: to show ourselves.
A normal young person can have a profile on numerous collective pages, from Facebook to Xanga, and can even join them with other services, such as Twitter or last.fm that offers a list of their music habits, then they can be included in a follow-up system such as FriendFeed or Blip.fm, you can also have a blog, in which the most recent photo galleries that are stored in the Flickr or the Pic
We can know numerous cases from which it is clear that for example the bride, seeing the flow of photographs the following morning of the common friends, finds out with who spent the previous night her fraudulent boyfriend or can fire the employee of a company because she writes her sincere opinion in her blog about the direction of the company: one thing is sure, the definition of private life was completely revalued.
A person’s online life is what she shows about herself – this is the definition behind the behavior of our day’s youth.
And whoever wants to hide something, or at least intends to dodge Google’s monopoly, can do so (starting for example with the Scroogle that uses Google’s search system, but leaves no traces).
There are many people who don’t want to sign up on collective pages to prevent them from being found, but you can replace Google’s “on-line” apps, from text writing software to news imaging and reading apps with alternative versions that don’t connect with gigantic servers or prepare the most perfect profile possible about us.
Public opinion almost expect that openly the day when Google shows its true face.
The company with its current value of 156 billion dollars is worth more than IBM (140 billion dollars), Intel (124 billion dollars) or Coca-Cola (110 billion dollars), AdWords/AdSense advertising surfaces threaten the revenues of advertising agencies, while services that are being introduced more and more quickly cause serious headaches not only for Microsoft, but also numerous other software developers.
Critical observers, however, will find alarming contradictions as well: for example the senior management strongly rejected the protest of the employees after doubling the price of the company’s kindergarten nursery, considered too expensive the unlimited number of food of the employees, but all this is nothing compared to the fact that in 2006 the Google gave in to pressure from the Chinese government and the company according to the agreement leaked all information that violated the good morality
One of the internal regulations of the company says that they will not announce any new services in advance, but only when it was already ready to work, what is certain is that the foreseeable problems of the coming months and years will be able to revolve to the World: while some believe that the project of scanning and archiving of Google books and magazines will acquire such dimensions that the company will soon be cited by the U.S
And the fact that Google is going to create a genetic database will be able to provide a good raw material for the writers of sci-fi, the Scroogled, novel of Cory Doctorow’s popular, describes in an Orthelian way that future, in which a man only of Google’s data can be described alarmingly well.
Two minors helped erase the perpetrator of the double murder of the city of Ózd.
Police questioned two minors about the double murder of Ózd who, according to informed suspicion, helped erase the traces of the crime - the spokesman of the General Policing Commissariat of Borsod province said on Tuesday.
The young women recognized the crime against them, and they are currently accused of the perpetrators of the crime.
The two minors - according to the Hungarian News Agency reports, are two girls - will be able to defend themselves free.
For complicity they can receive up to 5 years in prison.
The defendant of Ozd’s double murder — a 23-year-old man — has been in pre-trial detention since Sunday.
He is accused of murdering several people with premeditation and greed.
During the investigations it was revealed that the 23-year-old owed a large sum to a 53-year-old man.
The defendant didn’t want to pay his debt, that’s why on Wednesday last week he summoned his creditor to the headquarters of an Ózd company, where he killed him and then killed the victim’s 9-year-old daughter.
According to MTI reports, the young man prepared much earlier to perpetrate the crime, as he committed the murder with a weapon previously hidden in the crime scene.
The police analyze with an expert to the weapon and the circumstances of its use.
Warsaw Stock Exchange Unveiled Offer to Buy the Prague Stock Exchange
The Warsaw Stock Exchange offered two hundred million euros – about five billion Czech kroners – by one hundred percent of the shares of the Prague Stock Exchange.
Ludwik Sobolewski, president of the Warsaw Stock Exchange confirmed the offer made by the Poles, even though the Czechs have previously excluded the Warsaw Stock Exchange from the possible new owners of the Prague Stock Exchange.
The reason is that the Warsaw Stock Exchange is in the hands of the state.
99 percent of the shares are in the hands of the Polish state that within a few months wants to sell 60 percent of them.
The Czech economic newspaper E15 reported that the supply of the Poles has been the highest among those offered by those interested by the Prague Stock Exchange.
According to the Czech press, the Vienna Stock Exchange, the Nasdaq Transatlantic Stock Exchange, the New York Stock Exchange, the London Stock Exchange and Deutsche Börse have so far been offered.
Petr Koblic, the head of the Prague Stock Exchange declared last week that among those interested the worst new owner would be the Warsaw Stock Exchange and did not rule out the possibility that with it, in the future the Prague Stock Exchange disappeared.
Experts calculate the value of the Prague Stock Exchange at about 5 to 10 billion kroners.
Under the shareholder agreement it could sell approximately 90 percent of the shares.
The majority owner of the Prague Stock Exchange is the investment bank Patria Finance with a stake of approximately 25 percent, followed by Banco Ceská Sporitelna with 14.7 and the Tiger Holding Four S. a.r.l. with 13.5 percent.
On the financial crisis from the point of view of the European press
The main European newspapers in their comments on Tuesday dedicated to the increasingly profound international financial crisis speak of a "second September 11".
The global financial catastrophe is due to the American president - the Republic of Rome thinks - the president has not even been able to get the support of his own party for the hastily done bill, whose objective is to solve this hopeless situation...
Instead of a new “Pearl Habor,” which billionaire investor Warren Buffett was talking about, it’s more right to talk about a “september 11.”
According to a part of Madrid’s press, Washington is the scapegoat.
In El Mundo’s view the mistake of the political leadership of the United States was the one that brought the world economy to the edge of the abyss.
The danger of crumbling of the U.S. monetary system is increasingly growing and this will have an impact on the entire world.
Although Bush’s plan wasn’t perfect, after the congressional vote, there is a danger that Washington doesn’t offer a political instrument to deal with the crisis.
The world economy is suspended in the air - precisely when one of the greatest transformations in the history of capitalism takes place.
This threat cannot be disregarded - the Tages-Anzeiger of Geneva points out.
Some states today can still throw lifebeat to wobbly financial institutions, being able to save them from bankruptcy with taxpayer money.
But if, as the Dominos crumble even more banks, then neither the new funds, nor the new improvisations will be enough.
Long-term European Union member states need to put aside their nationalist selfishness and centralize control over fragmented financial markets.
The financial institutions in crisis received only more than 100 billion euros on Monday - recalls the Viennese Der Standard, adding that there are more and more real concerns that, as the Americans did, also European taxpayers will have to pay a lot of money to solve the crisis.
The EU so far has not dealt seriously with the crisis that happens as a cuname through the Old Continent .
"Saviors" won't have to immediately file hundreds of millions of euros, but it would be good if they defined: in what cases is it justified to use taxpayer funds to avoid greater evil?
Intelligent car mimics beef flight
What would be the best method to develop technologies in order to avoid collisions, if not the imitation of obstacle sensors existing in nature?
For example, that of bumblebees.
In a surprising project presented at Japan’s CEATEC, the bumblebees gave the starting point for Nissan engineers to design the next generation of collision prevention systems.
The Nissan, in cooperation with the University of Tokyo, designed nature-mimicking BR23C-type car robotic steering system, which was given the characteristics of bumblebees, with the ultimate goal of creating a system that can dodge all collisions.
During the flight each bumblebee creates its own particular oval space that actually looks a lot like our protective safety capsule - he explained in the exhibition Kazuhhiro Doi, technology director of RP and development and research.
They play an important role the compound eyes of bumblebees that they are able to see in all directions at an angle greater than 300 degrees.
To copy the function of the composite eyes, the engineers used the laser length measurement system.
This identifies the obstacles in front of the BR23C within a distance of 2 meters, at an angle of 180 degrees, calculates its distance and sends a signal to the microprocessor of the vehicle that immediately transforms into a maneuver to avoid the collision.
In a fraction of seconds the obstacle is identified, then the robot of the vehicle mimicking the movements of the bumblebees, modifies the direction by turning the wheels to the extent necessary.
Unliked to any existing system today, this manoeuvre is totally instinctive.
"If it didn't, the vehicle's robot couldn't react quickly enough to dodge obstacles," explains Toshiyuki Andoh, head of the Mobility Lab and vehicle robot project.
It must react immediately and instinctively, since this technology corresponds to the most vulnerable inner layer of the protective safety capsule, in a layer within which all kinds of collisions are currently considered unavoidable.
The whole process must reflect what a bumblebee does to dodge other bumblebees.
This process should be done in the blink of an eye.
However, unlike bumblebees, the movement cannot be directed upward, downward or diagonally, but can only be two-dimensional and exclusively in the direction of rotation of the wheels
In this way, instead of the infinite possibilities that exist for bumblebees to dodge other bumblebees, here they only used as a possibility for the robot of the car the rotary movement and acceleration also the braking.
BR23C uses lithium-polymer batteries that are lighter and their energy density is higher, which means that they have a longer lifetime than lithium-ion.
According to Andoh, the important thing is the instinctive and intelligent reaction and not the processing capacity of the data, let alone that of storage.
This device in every second should only process some input signals and react as appropriate.
It is not necessary to store this data or react with an instinctive logic based on the data of the previous maneuvers, so it uses only a few tens of kilobytes of memory.
No gigabyte memory or megabytes are needed.
This is the first step to develop the technology to immediately dodge the obstacles, which according to Nissan calculations, within ten years can be incorporated into the models manufactured in series.
Another possibility for its application is to incorporate the unit into the GPS satellite navigation system to bring the driver to their destination, dodging the obstacles in their path.
He already has a name for this very expensive child
The written version of the US$ 700 billion financial bailout package has been prepared to be applied in several phases in order to purchase bad credits from banks.
In the first phase, half of the money will be spent.
According to Eastern Coast schedules during new consultations that lasted until after midnight on Saturday, congressional leaders reached an agreement on the 700 billion-dollar financial bailout package, after several days of discussion.
“We’ve made significant progress — Nancy Pelosi, D-U.S. President of the U.S. congress, said, stating that there’s only a need to formalize the agreement into a document.
The commitment made on the package was supported by both presidential candidates, Barack Obama and John McCain.
Henry Paulson, the Minister of Finance, speaking about the outcome of the commitment stated: this program will work and will be efficient but other measures are needed. According to Pelosi, it is not a question of saving Wall Street, but of turning around the economy.
The written version of the package was published before the opening of the Asian markets, that is on Sunday before 8 pm, according to Washington’s schedule (that is before two o’clock on Monday, according to Central European hours), without causing a spectacular jump in the bags.
Regarding the law called emergency law for economic stabilization of the year 2008, on Monday, the U.S
President George W. Bush on Saturday night consulted with Pelosi and then the White House also welcomed the news about the deal.
“We are pleased with the progress made overnight and highly appreciate the efforts of both parties to stabilize our financial markets and protect our economy,” White House spokesman Tony Fratto said.
The program is different from the Bush administration’s original proposal to spend all 700 billion dollars to buy shares of poor-quality credit fund values.
Now only half of the 700 billion dollars can be spent, using 250 billion immediately after Congress votes, probably on Monday, the Ministry of Finance will buy securities of credit fund values, of bad rating and the fate of another 100 billion dollars depends on the president’s decision.
This program will be controlled by a special body, in which the president of the Federal Reserve will also participate.
Another half of US$700 billion can be spent after a new congressional decision.
According to the law the Ministry of Finance can apply a combined tactic: it will be able to simultaneously buy bad credits, mortgages and credit fund securities, in addition to other "poisonous" credits as well.
The purchase can be made in auctions or directly - reported competent persons of the ministry.
The law allows the affected companies to participate in an insurance program where the finance portfolio guarantees the worrying elements, for which the companies will pay the amount corresponding to the foreseeable damages.
Henry Paulson said: The law thus ensures the necessary financial means, that even 700 billion dollars can arrive to meet the urgent needs of the American financial system, whether it is the purchase of bad financial means, its assurance or the prevention of risks that could lead to the crumbling of some large financial institutions.
We do everything necessary to be ready to introduce the law as soon as they sign it - he added.
On the other hand, the heads of the banks that are in distress and waiting for the help of the State will be able to count on the official limitation of their compensations, which the U.S. argot calls simply golden parachutes.
Only in certain cases will payments be limited, and limitations depend on the form of assistance of the Ministry of Finance.
The limitation means that if the ministry buys in the framework of an auction, an extra tax will be imposed on gold parachutes, unless the bank’s failed boss retires.
By directly buying the bad credits the government will intervene aggressively to ensurce that bosses’ indemnities are not exaggerated.
In addition to existing gold parachute contracts will not be changed, the limitations refer only to new contracts to also stimulate participation in the programme.
This is the first case in U.S. history that a legal constraint will be in place for directors-general revenues - said Democrat Barney Frank, chairman of the congressional committee responsible for financial services.
The State will also have the right to acquire shares of the banks participating in the program, thus reducing the risk of the taxpayers, since in short they will be able to even obtain profits with the transaction as soon as the economy is recovered and with it the bank.
According to the bill in the next five years, the president must submit to Congress a proposal on how to return taxpayers the losses of the financial sector.
Of course on both sides there were those who expressed their reservations regarding the project.
It’s not what U.S. citizens entrusted to us, that i.e. they’ren’t protecting taxpayer dollars — California Republican Congressman Darrell Issa said.
His fellow Democrat of Ohio, Mary Kaptur, said: The measures were urged by those who are responsible for the crumbling of Wall Street.
Industrial prices continue to rise
In the month of August 2008, domestic industrial sales prices increased by 0.1 percent compared to last month’s prices and 12.9 percent compared to August 2007 prices – the Central Bureau of Statistics (KSH) reported.
Industrial export prices rose by 1.1 percent compared to those in July 2008 and decreased by 3.9 percent compared to the previous year.
And as a result of changes in domestic and export prices, industrial production prices increased by 0.7 percent over the previous month and 3.2 percent over the previous year.
Industrial sales prices increased only to a minimum extent, with 0.1 percent.
The domestic sales prices of the sectors of the processing industry increased minimally, with 0.1 percent compared to July.
The largest increase in the magnitude of prices occurred in August 2008, in the leather and footwear production sector (2.8 percent), due in the first place to the 4.6 percent monthly increase in bags and belts and the 2.5 percent increase in footwear.
The higher price level of plastic and chemical base materials resulted in a significant monthly increase in the prices of the branch of production of chemical materials (1.6 percent).
There was a decrease in price in the petrochemical sector, (1.4 percent), in the production of electrical machines and instruments (0.9 percent), as well as - in a minimal measure - in the wood processing sectors (0.1 percent).
They didn’t change the prices of papermaking, publishers, and printing precinces.
In the rest of the sectors of the processing industry there was an increase in prices between 0.2 and 0.9 percent.
In the supply of electricity, gas, heat and water that represent a significant peso within domestic trade, an increase of 0.3 percent was registered in August, firstly as a result of the effect of the increase in official prices from July 1.
In a comparison of a twelve-month period - in domestic sales of the processing industry sectors - the largest price increase was recorded in the petrochemical sector (32.4 percent).
In the metal processing sectoor there was an increase of 13.2 percent, while in the food, beverage and tobacco industry, of determining weight, there was an increase of 11 percent.
There was a decrease in prices in the textile industry (2.5 percent), as well as in the manufacture of electrical machines and instruments (0.3 percent).
In the rest of the processing sectors the pace of price growth was between 0.6 and 9.1 percent.
During the past year in the processing industry globally, prices increased by 10.2 percent.
The prices of electricity, the supply of gas, heat and water exceeded the prices of the previous year with 18.7 percent.
In the month of August, among the different sectors of domestic trade the largest monthly increase in prices (0.7 percent) was recorded in the sectors of investment goods.
In the consumer goods sectors, prices increased by 0.3 percent, in the prices of the energy sector and the intermediary sectors there were no changes compared to the previous month.
In August 2008, with respect to the same month of the previous year, the greatest price increase occurred in the energy sectors and in the intermediary industry (16.8 percent).
There was a decline of 6.8 percent in consumer goods and 1.4 per cent in investment goods.
Industry export prices calculated in HUF rose 1.1 percent over the previous month, and compared to 12 months, there was a 3.9 percent decline.
The price of our national currency in a month fell by 1.7 percent compared to the euro and by 7.1 percent compared to the dollar, compared to August 2007 strengthened by 7.5 percent compared to the euro and 15.9 percent against the dollar.
Next year won’t you need a visa to go to the U.S?
Kinga Göncz believes that there are many possibilities for the American-Hungarian agreement on the exemption of visas to enter into force around January 12 - the foreign minister talked about it in Chicago, in front of the Hungarian residents there.
In his opinion, "practically everything depends on whether the electronic access and control system is built in time on the other side of the Atlantic."
At the same time he warned that in the new system the entry prize will disappear, but tourists before their departure from the country of origin must register.
As of today the head of Hungarian diplomacy holds talks in Washington.
He will meet with Secretary of State Condoleezza Rice by handing over the Median Cross with the Star of the Order of Merit of the Republic of Hungary and will hold negotiations with the international policy advisers of the presidential candidates, Democrat Barack Obama and Republican John McCain.
Both Barack Obama and McCain are in favor of the banks’ financial bailout package.
Barack Obama and John McCain, both candidates for the presidency of the two major U.S. parties on Sunday secured their support for the administration’s 700-million-dollar banking aid program
The representatives of the Congress and of the administration, after several marathon-type negotiations, in the early hours of Sunday announced: an early agreement was reached on the financial rescue package of the banks.
The financial package aimed at solving the Wall Street crisis and thawing the frozen credit market became the central issue of the presidential election campaign.
Both Obama and McCain want to show that they are more capable than their rival to get the country out of the economic crisis.
According to the most recent polls, when economic issues were brought to the forefront, Obama regained some advantage and the advantage of McCain that he had obtained after the convention of the Republicans with the candidacy of Sarah Palin to the vice presidency disappeared.
At a Detroit campaign rally last Sunday, Obama expressed his hope that Congress will quickly pass the US$700 billion-dollar package bill.
He stressed that the proposal includes those points of consumer protection, which he himself supported.
"We have to act now and responsibly . . . is jeopardizing the employment, saving of you whole industries and the stability of the entire economy," he told a crowd of 35 thousand people.
He didn’t miss the opportunity to qualify McCain’s economic concepts obsolete.
In an interview with ABC, McCain explained that "we will all swallow this hard ... but doing nothing is simply not a viable path."
The Republican senator said that the proposal includes the establishment of a commission of control to the finance minister and the limitation of the compensation of the executives, he was the one who insisted on that.
Obama told CBS that McCain did not play any important role in the consultations, but he consulted with the minister on a daily basis.
Congressional President Nancy Pelosi said Sunday that congressmen are likely to vote on the bill on Monday.
Press review of the German-spoking area
The right-wing group is intact, only within the group itself became the most conscientious voters - says Der Spiegel about CSU's weak election result in Bavaria.
Haider and his followers are ready to rule in Austria to prevent a red-and-white coalition.
Der Spiegel (spiegel.de)
In the electronic issue of the left-wing German magazine Franz Walter, in his article entitled "The Bavarian Revolution devours his parents" he analyzes the motives for the dramatic defeat of the CSU.
According to the well-known polythologist, CSU erosion had started long before the sad duo Beckstein-Huber had taken office.
The Social Christians for several decades were developing to Bavaria - and now precisely these modern citizens are those who turn their backs on him.
The change of an era is at the same time a problem of the whole of Christian democracy, as well as Angela Merkel.
The failure was not totally surprising for the CSU, but on Sunday a process that had been foreseen for almost ten years was completed: the indisputable hegemony of a state match disappeared.
Ten years ago, in 1998 the CSU obtained 47.7 percent, for the first time below 50 percent since the 1950s.
This was repeated three years ago, in the 2005 Bundestag elections, that is to say even during the above-mentioned Stoiber era.
The reason for this is the consequent modernization of the CSU in the devouring province of its parents .
Sociologists have been predicting this 40 years ago, but in the rhythm they were very wrong. However, the secularization, the results of education and the settlement of the North Germans in the developed regions of Bavaria had their negative consequences on the fidelity of CSU voters.
Modernization also increases the possibilities and this also has political consequences.
The right-wing group is intact, only within the group itself became the most conscious, most critical, and more stubborn voters.
It is surprising that in recent weeks precisely the conventional groups of the citizens were those who moved further away from the CSU; the self-employed, the small industrialists, those who have a bachelor’s degree and the graduates.
This resulted in less than 40 percent support for the CSU.
Die Presse (diepresse.com)
Vienna's conservative newspaper: "Who with whom? In its article entitled "Party presidents are very reserved on coalition issues" - deals with the confusing situation of domestic politics after the Austrian elections.
SPÖ wants to negotiate with the ÖVP.
The ÖVP prohibits the SPÖ from intruding its internal affairs.
The BZÖ is open in all directions to negotiate, the Greens on the other hand still do not want to make consultations about the coalition.
The elections have already been held, now everything revolves around the coalition; in the debate held on public television, the leaders of the parties barely allowed to see something of their decks.
Werner Faymann, the SPÖ president, confirmed that he wants to negotiate with the ÖVP.
The SPÖ wants to demonstrate that collaboration between the two parties is possible - this already exists in some provinces and social associations.
Fayman left pending the question that if he can imagine a coalition with Wilhelm Molterer, the current president of the ÖVP, in the position of vice chancellor.
He claimed that in any case they disapproved the Schüssel-Molterer era.
It is not possible to follow this political trend.
Molterer reacted cautiously to the red offers.
He said that cooperation will surely not be successful if Faymann tries to meddle in the internal affairs of the ÖVP.
It is still open in the party whether they will elect the opposition or enter the coalition, these issues must undoubtedly be discussed, within the ÖVP itself.
BZÖ President Jörg Haider was open in all directions.
"To prevent the red-black coalition, we are willing to take responsibility for the government," Haider said.
Járóka: The vicious circle of poverty and segregation must be broken
Today the European Summit for Equal Opportunities has begun in Paris, its host is France that this year is also President of the European Union.
Lívia Járóka, deputy of the European People’s Party for Fidesz, in her message addressed to the plenary, as one of the main speakers of this professional meeting, drew attention to segregation in education, because it is one of the most serious violations that plague Roma children and is also the greatest obstacle to the prevalence of their interests.
This high-level conference was inaugurated – on behalf of the French presidency – by Xavier Bertrand, French Minister of Employment and Social Affairs and by Vladimir Spidla, European Commissioner responsible for jobs, social affairs and equal opportunities.
Representatives of governments, European social partners and representatives of the most important European social rights organisations attended the meeting.
Járóka - according to the press bureau of the Fidesz group of deputies in the European Parliament - warned that in addition to discrimination in employment, Gypsies are left out of the labour market in the first place because of their low level of schooling.
"Most young Gypsies have not completed secondary education and due to the poor quality of basic education, only an insignificant part can obtain a university diploma."
Járóka also stressed that education, as a fundamental human right, has a decisive role in the prevalence of other human rights as well.
Investment in the education of Roma children at an early age can strengthen the economy of the Member States of the European Union.
According to the MEP, it is necessary to widely raise awareness of these issues both among Gypsies and among non-Gypsies.
Well, the earlier a Gypsy student starts school, the more likely it is to become an active member of the labor market; through income and consumption taxes they will also contribute to the national budget.
"Gypsies, as citizens of the European Union, must be assured of the right to quality education and ensure the abolition of segregated and low-level education," said Lívia Járóka.
According to the MEP, the objective and active unity of the European Union is necessary in order to immediately accelerate the processes of school desegregation, for this the correct implementation of existing and planned anti-discrimination directives is of fundamental importance.
"The vicious circle of poverty, segregation and unemployment must be disrupted, we must offer Gypsy children the possibility guaranteed by the democratic space so that they can contribute to the future of Europe as citizens of full rights," Járóka demanded.
The objective of the European Summit for Equal Opportunities organized annually since last year's Berlin meeting in the sign of the "European Year of Equal Opportunities", is to ensure a unique forum to promote the abolition of discrimination and equal opportunities at European and national level in the Member States.
CSU: grace for a transitional period
At the end of October a decision will be made on the fate of the unsuccessful Huber-Beckstein duo
Despite the serious electoral defeat, heads have not yet been cut into the summits of the Bavarian CSU, for the moment the debate on personal issues has been postponed.
Erwin Huber, president of the party and Günther Beckstein, provincial prime minister are still in office, but it is not known when grace will last.
The fate of the duo, who suffered a catastrophic electoral defeat of 17 percent, will be decided in the extraordinary congression of the party to be held on the last weekend of October.
The members of the much-criticized duo hinted: they don’t cling so much to their positions.
With this they intended to reassure the furious members of their parliamentary group and their grassroots organization, who a day after the "Bavarian tsunami" demanded personal consequences due to the loss of the absolute majority.
Five years ago - although under the direction of Edmund Stoiber who was at the height of his career - the Christian social union reached 60.7 percent, instead now, a year afterested against Stoiber, they achieved only 43.4 percent.
CSU for 46 years had "monopoly" in Bavaria giving 18 percent of German GDP.
Although in the southern province, of key importance to the Hungarian economy, conservatives continue to predominate, in the future they will certainly have to coalition with someone.
As the first sign of the party’s restructuring, Vice-President Horst Seehofer, the federal minister of agriculture, one of Huber’s possible successors, also has a position in the small intelligence group that begins negotiations with the liberal FDP and the right-wing Free Electors about a possible government coalition in Munich.
The strange thing about fate is that Gabriele Pauli, whose performance against Stoiber was exploited for the coup of the duo Huber-Beckstein and then cruelly erased from the stage the ambitious local politician on the stage.
CSU’s top leaders are now investing all their energies to stabilize Beckstein.
In the transition he will receive an active Stoiber role also that until now he has been moving the ropes in the background, the former provincial head of government and former president of the CSU called September 28 the bitterest day of his political career.
On Monday Huber made some critical remarks to the CDU, in his opinion they would have deserved much more support from the sister party.
Other CSU politicians interpreted defeat as a warning to the CDU and Angela Merkel herself as well.
After the Bundestag’s September 2009 elections, Merkel will not be able to be chancellor if they are not able to unveil together the CSU who played a momentous role in the successes of the 2005 national elections.
According to Merkel who could barely hide her disappointment at the failure, CSU’s losses won’t have a negative impact on the Berlin grand coalition.
Which is naturally relative: it won't be easier to treat the wounded CSU and the ongoing social democratic crisis.
The SPD with its 18.6 percent achieved its worst result since 1946 in Bavaria.
Lukashenko's opposition: 110-0
After Sunday’s elections, there will be no oppositing MP in the Belarusian parliament.
According to Russian observers, this is explained by the well-being and stability guaranteed in the country by Alexandr Lukashenko, instead according to the Organization for Security and Cooperation in Europe (OSCE), this is explained rather by the violations of the law committed during the counting of the votes.
The OSCE, which sent 450 observers from 43 countries, did not recognize the election result.
Although the country’s legislature of 10 million inhabitants, made up of one hundred and ten deputies, more than a decade ago has no opposition, before yesterday’s elections the united opposition under the name of the United Democratic Forces (ODSZ) hoped that Lukashenko, who for the fourth time renewed his mandate after the 2006 elections of dubious legitimacy
So the ODSZ suppressed the boycott it originally wanted to do.
At the bottom of the expectations of the opposition was that Belarus, which is increasingly dependent on Russia - which took credit to moderate the importation of natural gas increasingly expensive from Russia and that contributed to the sale to Russia of the Beltransgaz, owner of the gas pipeline that passes through the country - wished to improve its relations with the European Union, which does not give entry to Lukashenko and the other high-level politicians
It was a sign of detente when the OSCE, when evaluating the electoral campaign, placed emphasis rather on positive phenomena and not on mistakes - such as the prohibition on participation imposed on a third of opposition candidates.
However Monday’s OSCE primary report criticized even the campaign itself — in which opposition candidates couldn’t appear in the press — and especially that the opposition couldn’t be present in the vote count.
With all this in the opinion of the opposition it feels an improvement in the political climate: political prisoners were released and Minsk is ready for a small confrontation with Moscow, denying the recognition of the separation of South Ossetia and Abhasia from Georgia, although Russia - with which Belarus theoretically constitutes a federal state - already a month ago that considers the two regions as independent.
"We've taken two steps forward and one back, but most importantly the dialogue between Belarus and the European Union has begun," Alexandr Milinkevich said.
According to the opposition candidate of the 2006-606 presidential elections it is desirable to maintain this situation, even though "the regime fears to allow the entry of even an opponent in that parliament without weight."
The opposition does not plan to organize protest demonstrations by seeing the results, rather trying to convey to voters its message about the need for economic reforms.
- This clearly causes us many problems because we must print the opposition press in Russia, the local authorities put difficulties before its distribution, but even so I see that more and more are those who support change among seniors as well - said Milinkevich, referring to the fact that the Lukashenko regime, which believes that its main result is the creation of social security, they do not deem it adequate or even the retirees, who are officially the most subsidized.
Due to the indebtedness of the country and the increase in the trade deficit, it is only a matter of time the decomposition of social security that "looks like the silence of cemeteries" - Milinkevich said.
Russian observers opposed to the opposition politician called the elections democratic.
Sergei Lebedev, head of the mission of the Commonwealth of Independent States, told the Russian news agency Ria Novosti: "people do not believe in words but in deeds", so that the lack of opposition is nothing more than the testimony of the maturity of the Belarusian voters.
Brunetta: "From now on you have breakfast before you start working"
It has never happened in the history of Palacio Chigi to put automatic doors to control the entry and exit of the personnel.
but from today it starts with this measure against who signs and then goes to the bar to have a coffee in working hours.
This novelty has been presented today by the Minister of the Public Administration, Renato Brunetta and the Secretary General of the Presidency of the Council, Mauro Masi.
“Automatic doors – says Brunetta – are an instrument to work better, with greater productivity, more presence and more services,” the minister says.
"A new season of accountability and transparency now opens up.
This is Reformism," Brunetta again emphasizes.
With Palacio Chigi the installation is completed in all the buildings of the Presidency of the Council.
For Masi "the choice of automatic doors is also important from the symbolic point of view".
There has been no resistance from employees, says the secretary general: "it has been a change shared by the workers and there was the collaboration from them."
In short, no more breakfast during working hours; no more coffee and crescents.
Brunetta's word, which suggests, smiling, "a good cappuccino at 7 in the morning is a holy hand."
During a convention at the High School of Public Administration
From Rome, the minister declares that "in three months the absences due to diseases of public employees have been reduced by 50%, it means 60 thousand more people to work in a year."
And he adds that it is necessary to render the Public Administration more effective
Italian, "which wage dynamics - explains the minister - in the last 8-10 years have been double compared to the private sector and well above the rate of inflation."
For now millions of public employees have come together to oppose the rules of the Brunetta decree adhering to the request supported by the Codacons.
"While the Minister of the Civil Service shows the numbers, the slightest absenteeism of work for causes of disease - writes the association of consummators - the people of 'lazy workers' is constantly increasing.
There are millions effectively in Italy the correct and productive public administration employees who have come together to declare war on the illegitimate rules of the decree."
In particular, the Tar will answer the exclusion of added economic treatments due to illness due to service; the extension of the hourly belts in which the medical control visits of the sick employee are carried out, and other aspects contained in the new provisions desired by the minister.
Labour Accidents, Napolitano: "Crucial Prevention"
Every day, in Italy, 2,500 accidents are verified at work, 3 people die and 27 are permanently invalid.
By 2007, Inail data effectively confirm that white deaths have been approximately 1,200.
Figures that testify to the seriousness of a phenomenon that is one of the main causes of death and causes almost twice the deaths compared to homicides.
To attract the attention of the institutions, social forces and the media on this dramatic issue, today the Anmil celebrates in all the provinces of Italy the 58th national day for the victims of workplace accidents, institutionalized on the second Sunday of October.
"The worrying data released by the Anmil and the same tragic news of these days confirm how crucial the question of prevention at work is, "says the president of the Republic Giorgio Napolitano, in the message sent to the president of the Anmil, National Association mutilated and disabled by the work, Pietro Mercandelli.
The head of state expresses his "great appreciation for the constant associative commitment in favor of prevention in the workplace, the protection of injured workers, the assistance to the families of the victims and the awareness of public opinion."
"It has been manifested, an 'enough', sincerely shared, in the face of tragedies that, due to their dimensions, provoke the cry of the media and the participation of public opinion, instead the daily reality proposes dramatic cases, even repeated in their dynamics."
Napolitano does not hide that "there is undoubtedly a problem of resources: it is decisive to invest in training and information.
Particular significances take the many initiatives promoted in the school environment for more direct awareness on the part of young people entering the world of work.
It is a duty to keep attention to the phenomenon alive, not to curb the alarm about social gravity, to apply and improve legislative norms.
For his part, the president of the Gianfranco Fini Chamber has stressed "how the phenomenon of white deaths constitute an absolute social emergency, which offends the conscience of each of us and imposes on all the institutions a determined effort to urgently put an end."
"The data on accidents at work seem to indicate a slight positive approach, but this does not mean that the number of white deaths is equally impressive," said Anmil President Pietro Mercandelli.
"We don't really want this "trend to decline" to translate into less attention, because it's precisely when the attention diminishes that tragedy explodes.
"We believe that at the general level it is still done too little to contrast the phenomenon of accidents and the remedy can be exercised through multiple actions.
They are necessary, in our opinion - Mercandelli has stressed - greater controls and inspections, but also a stronger intervention on the training of workers, and this from the world of school."
"Serves a further effort - he added - as far as communication and public awareness is concerned.
But, above all, it serves a greater sense of responsibility on the part of employers regarding a phenomenon that represents a social emergency."
Mercandelli has denounced "the progressive deterioration of the level of subsidiary guardianship foreseen for the victims of work" and the "assistance referral to which the system is heading in recent years".
"The objective is to restore the worker the insurance guarantee - he has added - because the fate of those who are accidental do not have to depend on the gift arranged by the legislator each time."
Mp3 Readers Under Accuse, Put Hearing at Risk
Hearing high-volume music for a long period of time using portable music devices such as Mp3 readers can cause permanent hearing injuries.
This is what the European Commission says, which in a communiqué released in Bruxel cites the opinion of the Scientific Commission of the emerging and recently identified (Csrseri) of the EU, published today.
"From this scientific opinion - it reads in the note - it arises that 5-10% of those who, for a period of at least 5 years, listen to music with portable musical devices weekly for more than an hour a day having the device at high volume risk a permanent loss of hearing."
"I'm concerned that such a high number of young people who often use portable music devices and high acoustic cell phones can unconsciously ruin their ears irretrievably," says Meglena Kuneva.
“From the scientific evidence – Ue responsibility follows – a clear risk emerges and we must react quickly.
What counts, is sensitizing the consumers and rendering this information in the public domain.
We must also re-examine existing control systems in the light of this scientific opinion, so that they are broadly effective and take the plunge with the new technology."
Bruxel had asked the Independent Scientific Committee to examine the problem, seeing the great use of portable musical devices and the increase in the number of young people exposed to the noise that originates.
"Scientists "convey Executive Ue - confirm that it is cause for concern and the European Commission will now examine together with member states and stakeholders what measures could eventually be taken to better protect children and teenagers from exposure to noise coming from portable musical devices and related devices."
Currently, there is already a European safety standard that limits to 100 dB the noise level of portable musical appliances, but concern increases as auditory damage that can result from excessive exposure to such noise sources.
It is possible to greatly limit these damages by resorting to solutions such as the reduction in noise levels and exposure time.
In its view, the Ue Scientific Committee makes it clear that users of portable musical devices listen at high volume (more than 89 decibels)musics for only 5 hours a week exceed the current limit in force relative to the maximum spoiled noise at the workplace.
Those who listen to music in such conditions for longer periods, risk a permanent loss of hearing after a period of 5 years.
It means that it affects 5-10% of users of such devices and the number can be quantified between 2.5 and 10 million people in EU.
Rome, Alemanno gives way to the Commission for the future of the capital
Today begins, in March is closed, in June the accounts will be made.
This is the calendar set by the Municipality and for the workers of the "Commission for the Futute of the capital of Rome", which was established this morning in its new headquarters behind the Baths of Caracalla.
In six months, President Antonio Marzano and the other 49 members of the Commission will deliberate the main points for Rome.
Once the doors are closed in March, the board and the communal council will evaluate analyses and projects, in order to present in June the Strategic Piano for Rome with the "official bun" of the Municipality and its mayor Gianni Alemanno.
"The Commission is absolutely independent and is represented by all political, social and cultural ideas ♪ - it tends to underscore Germany ♪ - It must provide proposals for the development of Rome in which those who decide politically, the board and the municipal council, can then be endorsed.
There is no position of roles, only the will to have a place to elaborate a great project for Rome.
In March completed the works will disappear, because this experience must have an accurate temporary finish.
In June – the mayor announces – we will present the strategic plan using the work done by the Commission for the future of the capital of Rome.”
To those who accuse the Commission of useless, given that its opinions are not binding, Alemanno responds: "Everything depends on the work that will be in order to carry out the Commission and the quality of its proposals.
If the quality will be present, as well as in France with the Attali Commission and as I am also sure in Rome, its contribution will be fundamental.
Almost always the policy is crushed in the ordinary management and in emergencies that back in return are manifested.
On the contrary, we, on the contrary, want to look beyond and in the long term, in a more profound perspective, working seriously to the development of Rome and its future."
The mayor of Rome also tends to point out that "this Commission is neither a useless entity nor a banality: it is absolutely free, it does not coastal a euro to Roman citizens and will serve to involve and reason the best minds that the capital squeezes."
For Alemanno, indeed, "it is necessary to have a strategic design as a reference, not closed or immobile, to allow our city to make an authentic level jump, of which we have absolute necessity, thinking with a unitary spirit to its future."
A future that, specifies the mayor of Rome" will not only be limited to the current communal confines but will look beyond" not only in the perspective of the future metropolitan city and its legal state of Capital but "also considering the role that Rome can and must develop as the Capital of Europe and the Mediterranean".
Obama, the first anti-American president.
He has written an American political note that he is interested in going independent: "Barack Obama will be the second anti-American president.
The first was Jimmy Carter, who with his decisions reduced the USA economy and had relations (as it also does today gives a private citizen) with the enemy Islam."
Attacks on Obama are rising as the election date approaches.
A Miami lady wrote on a website: "This person is full of ambitions.
Obama has a big stone face: he thinks he’ll win the nation’s highest office he’s held by two governors and five black senators!”
They’re actually attacks that don’t say much; they’re clearly racial attacks and don’t respond to the voters’ question: will he be a good president? And there are also the polls; they all say that Obama won and with a good advantage.
Also in this case there is those who speak with the heart but not with the brain.
A newspaper of the Mississippi, in the bowels of the south of the United States, has written an editorial: once in the booth to vote we will know well to whom the American patriot will give his vote.
One side comes out of the American mentality covered to the last.
"Say whatever you want, we'll then think about where to put the cross, whether it's about Obama or McCain."
There are people who swear: if Obama wins, we will leave America.
Things ever said before now, that seems almost true the success of the black candidate.
Yet in spite of all these reasonings, the winning weapon for the democratic is George Bush.
They’ve asked 1500 people: what were the mistakes made by Bush during his tenure? 89 percent have replied: Iraq.
It Changes America.
In Vietnam this nation lost 50,000 soldiers and kicked her home in the butt.
In Iraq there are 4500 soldiers who have lost their lives and Americans have not been forced to make the bags.
Likewise, Iraq for the majority has been Bush’s weakness.
Whoever will assume George W’s position will have an enormous duty to unwrapped.
Use, economic collapse is also felt for journalists: in newspapers it's time for cuts. Many blame the Internet, "murderer" of printed paper.
Fifteen American journalists have been questioned by the PEW Research Center about the status of their profession and mind control for the future.
While today journalists are almost pessimistic about their future.
However, journalists have not openly declared feeling less concerned about credibility.
They don’t feel isolated as once.
The problem for American journalists is money, money.
The 2008 crisis for these journalists is a destroyed economic model crisis.
In addition the cuts made in the room where the editors work to carry out the newspaper, is a big problem.
It is a problem that must be solved, according to the journalists interviewed, if you don’t want traditional journalism as the majority of the public understands to be substantially reduced.
A clear but complex pessimism predominates today over the American journalist.
Six out of ten journalists and executives are convinced that journalism at the national level is following the wrong path.
In the local field the executive group is 65%.
Printed against emission.
It’s not hard for journalists to see where the website goes.
The largest publishing houses open a gap on the Internet, for many seen as the "murderer" of the printed letter.
The "economic pressure" that journalists warn has increased to 79%.
The 500 journalists interviewed have admitted that they are embracing technology in the hope "that it does something good" for journalism.
The biggest break today in American journalism is between those who run the newspapers – that is, the directors – and the journalists who work for them.
56% of executives at the national level are sure that their journalists share the same values, while at the local level the percentage drops to 23%.
For some this has to do with the "safety of work".
Executives who plan to lose their jobs in 3 years are 47% nationally.
For newspaper staff it is 30%.
“Safe labor” at staff level (our copywriters, ndr) in America is always on the agenda.
Only 13% of journalists work on a contract.
In an immense nation like the U.S., with 300 million inhabitants and millions of newspapers, magazines, radios, TV and the Internet, employers often offer what they want and thus become a matter of “take it or leave it.”
Directors almost always receive good salaries, while copywriters can earn up to 10 thousand dollars a month, plus retirement and social insurance.
For the holidays, the reasoning becomes complicated: a total of days the first year, another after the third to reach 15 full days after a certain number of years.
But American journalists, by their admission, become "sick" off during the year.
It's all a matter of climate.
UNIPOL: COURT OF ROME DANILO COPPOLA STAYS IN GROTTAFERRATA
The president of the second criminal section of the court of Rome, Carmelo Rinaudo, has decided to reject the instance of the real estate Danilo Coppola who had asked to be able to move from his city, Grottaferrata, to a room in the city of Rome.
Coppola is inquired by bankruptcy in the field of the investigation into the anti-pact related to Unipol-Bnl escalation.
In the course of the arrest process in charge, last week, he has obtained the house release, transforming it into compulsory residence to Grottaferrata.
His lawyers, Michele Gentiloni and Gaetano Pecorella, had asked that the real estate be able to travel the route of the city of the province to a room in the capital.
According to the court, these trips (by which the pm has given an opposite vote) would allow him to influence his society and access the evidence that accuses him.
Elites in Danger
The phenomenon had already manifested a few days ago with the vote of the camera of the representatives against the salvation plan of 700 million dollars launched by the White House: a significant part of Americans was, and this, more interested to punish Wall Street than to save the economy.
It gives us a confirmation yesterday’s New York Times informing us that the ongoing crisis is disarming the Republican party, always more divided between its old soul of the East Coast, moderate, favorable to the federal institutions and the business community, and its new soul, instead, conservative, hostile to “those of Washington” and to the world of finance, strong especially in the Central and Southern states.
The soul, in fact, which has become arrogant with the vote of one who spoke at the beginning.
This just quoted is just one example of the mutations, of the great mutations, which the ongoing economic earthquake announces: not only in the United States but in all of the West and not just here alone.
Whether in the United States as in Europe the crisis has long seemed to function as an accelerator of hatching phenomena that with the new climate solidifies and comes to light.
The first of these phenomena is re-updating, the extraordinary reactivation, of the state-sovereignty double category in relation to a type of nationalization of the economy.
The crisis, in fact, is a crisis of banking institutions - it would finance which have, yes, strong financial relations with abroad, but above all the balance sheets of families living in a single country and in a single state are much more compromised.
He who immediately creates a political problem for those who govern it: that is to say how to respond to the difficulty and protests of those people and of those families who, on the other hand, are voters.
The crisis appears economically globally but is politically and exclusively national.
Political internationalism seems substantially offside or they don’t have much to say: the crucial test is the European Union which is divided as always between the different interests and the different state strategies does not decide any common policy.
It is from the government of each state that everyone expects an intervention, rescue and reactivation plans, of new rules and above all the subsidy of funds: from the moment you get to the cut it is only the state that owns the economic resources and the mass of financing resources to remedy things.
And they also have the necessary means and the legitimacy to use them: two invaluable resources, securities in certain circumstances in which no market probably and no organization can ever dispose to the same extent.
This new emphasis that the crisis places on the nation-state is in perfect harmony, with the greatest importance whenever the new development of the economy tends to attribute it to a factor very colluded to that element: territoriality.
Paradoxically, while we were convinced that we have entered the network of ever more sophisticated technology, of the immaterial, while we were convinced that global finance was already destined to dominate the world, we realized that our future will instead have to make the accounts more and more with unimmaterial things such as water, crops and oil.
All things that, look, can certainly be transported from one place to the other of the earth but are equally united in absolute mode in a circumscribed space, a territory.
So those who are sovereign certainly have many more letters with respect to those who are not, and those who have the misfortune to live in a position without crops, without oil and without water.
I come to the second novelty that but foreshadows a fracture.
Who says Territory, State, Government, inevitably says Politics and Leadership.
In this sense the economic crisis seems to produce two converging phenomena.
On the one hand the objective awareness of the need for a leadership, the request of someone who knows how to take the situation.
On the other hand a wave of discredit for the existing leaderships, of inadequate economic species with many dark areas.
And together something deeper and in a somewhat disturbing sense: a discredit, an intolerance, an inadequate image, a sense of remoteness, which tends to implicate the entire ruling class of the countries of the West in an increasing number.
It seems to advance always more, in various places of the population, the conviction that before their actions are the same as those of the social elites so far on the rise, in the same way of feeling and of being, their culture in the comprehensive exception of the end, to have made one’s own time and to be stranger to the opinions of the majority.
The demand for leadership, in a nutshell, feeds underground a ramified but powerful movement of delegitimization of the ruling classes and traditional political structures, which are manifested in an "electoral revolt" or in the sudden changes of collective humors of recent times, from the conservative departure in Austria-Baviera to the collapse of the social-democratic consensus in Britain, to the rebellion of the men of the U.S
You have the impression that the traditional elites, their parties, their programs, but also their rites, their newspapers, their accredited intellectuals, their format would say some, always make more difficulty to understand and then to represent, what from today that is taking shape are the deep strata of Western society and that the economic crisis renews, increases and agitates potentially inordinately.
Faced with all this talking about a "mass rebellion" today is frankly exaggerated.
But having your eyes open certainly isn’t.
Super glue for walking on the walls
Overcoming the laws of gravity thanks to super glue and in the future walking on the walls as a spider man.
It’s the goal of several American research centers and now a team of four institutes has gotten pretty close.
With an adhesive of only 2.5 square centimeters, scientists have been able to hit a 100 kilo body on a vertical wall.
THE STUDY – The U.S. journal Science has published the discoveries of researchers from the University of Dayton, Akron, the Georgia Institute of Technology and the Air Force Research Laboratory.
The material invented by the research team is an evolution of existing ones that use a particular carbon structure, called carbon nanotubes.
“The glue principle can be imagined as a series of tubes sorted as a stack of spaghetti,” explains Zhong Lin Wang of Atlanta’s Georgia Institute of Technology.
Scientists have been inspired by the gesco legs, covered in microscopic hairs that can ensure the animal a perfect adhesion.
Testing made on different materials, such as glass, Teflon and sandpaper, have shown that the new adhesive is ten times more powerful from the legs of this reptile and at the same time "easily peels off the walls," explains Liming Dai, a researcher at the University of Dayton Engineering.
WALKING THROUGH THE WALLS? - "This material could be useful as a transitory adhesive" adds Liming Dai.
Layers to walk through the walls exactly as Spider-Man? Layers yes, but researchers think of a much less fascinating use as the connection between electronic devices, because carbon nanotubes are conductors of heat and electric current.
Other applications might have to do with aerospatial engineering.
At the moment, no superheroes.
OTHER RESEARCH - The University of Berkeley in California is also dedicated to finding a new adhesive.
In an article in the journal American Chemical Society, Californian scholars have presented an adhesive made from microfibers such as self-cleaning hair from dust during movement on a surface to always maintain perfect adhesion.
Drugs: Never with Fruit Juice
Attention to grapefruit juice, orange and apple juice.
These beverages, consumed especially in summer because they are refreshing and rich of vitamins, if taken contemporaneously with some drugs they are altered by amplifying or decreasing depending on the case, the efficiency with serious health consequences.
To repeat the risk of fruit juices are packaged that fresh associated with the assumption of some medicines David Bailey, a professor at the University of Western Ontario in London, who from the 236th national meeting of the American Chemical Society underway Philadelphia sends a new alarm: a glass of grapefruit, orange and apple juice suffices to reduce the absorption of some drugs, nullifying the beneficial effects and putting the health of patients at risk.
Grapefruit juice was already low-accused because it was held responsible for increasing some anti-arrhythmic, antibiotic, anxiolytic, anti-histamine and neurological medicinal levels to toxic levels.
DRUGS AT RISK – The same Italian drug agency had given the news in an information bulletin two years ago alarming doctors and patients not to underestimate the danger that derived from this mixture and to pay attention to something is drunk in the case a drug such as Diasepam or Metadone.
NOT JUSTLY THE GRIEF – According to experts, orange and apple juice also contain substances that inhibit drugs.
A long list of the active ingredients inhibited by grapefruit and other juices.
Hence Michele Carruba’s call, director of the pharmacology department of the State University of Milano: “These discoveries in general are pointed out to the various international and national drug agencies that eventually provide to change its information notes.
That is why we must always read the illustrative brochures of the medicines that are assumed and if there is something that is not clear to us, not to be impressed, to ask clearly the doctor or the pharmacist,” stressed the expert of the agency Ansa.
The Novel of Economics to Paul Krugman
The nobel economics award has been assigned to American Paul Krugman for his studies, his trade models, and the localization of economic activities.
Krugman, 55, is a neo-Keynesian who teaches Princeton University and is a New York Times editorialist.
Krugman is one of the biggest critics of the Bush administration’s decisions on economics and foreign policy.
A few months after the September 11, 2001 attack, Enron went bankrupt, Krugman had foreseen in an editorial published by the New York Times that the second event would be more decisive than the first, in ending as a consequence for the United States.
A foresight that triggers a lot of controversy and that for several years was reproached to the economy, but that has now been revealed exactly.
"I'm shocked and a little bit upset about how the memory of Enron and Worldcom's collapse scandal have quickly disappeared from public attention," Krugman said at the end of 2002.
According to Lorenzo Bini Smaghi of the executive committee of European central banking, Krugman is an "economist of great value", but also a publicizer with a "very aggressive style, particularly critical against the excesses of liberalism of the Bush administration".
Open Office, I echo the third edition of the "anti-Microsoft" package
It is the day of the launch of OpenOffice.org 3.0, the open source suite of personal productivity that sees to always attract more users, from home to the office to public administration professionals, as a free alternative to the well-known Microsoft Office.
After a work of almost a year by the volunteer developers, of which their backs are monitored by SUN Microsystem, the new Open Office is shown to the public with several novelties: to the welcome screen and to the less rude magazine interface, more consistent others are added, such as the compatibility for the Apple Mac OS X operating system and support for the new ODF(Open Document Format) 1.2 format, the latest ISO standard version.
Attention also to multi-operation with the Office 2007, Open Office suite is in order to open documents with the new Microsoft extension (.docx, .xlsx, .pptx).
Interesting some specific functions of some modules such as one that allows to reduce the dimension of the PowerPoint presentation, useful, for example, to send it via electronic post, or the possibility of importing the PDF file into the graphical elaboration module, preserving the original aspect of the page.
Always on this front you can create "Hybrid PDF" documents, which accumulate the typical graph of the Adobe format with the elements of a spreadsheet or text processor.
Collaboration is an element that has received different improvements within the applications: in the spreadsheet they can intervene in various users, avoiding the conflicts of the modifications, in the elaboration of texts, each collaborator is given a color in the comment for a better recognition in the review phase.
Some companies are also working to bring some OpenOffice features to the Web (on the cloud), and in the coming weeks they should give the definitive result.
The Italian version can be downloaded at http://it.openoffice.org/download/3.0.0/download300.html and was added to the English that was in the mirror since Friday.
In addition that for Windows and Mac OS, as normally the suite is also available for the Linux operating system.
On request you can also be sent the installation cd at home or at work.
And if the issue of free can be a hook for the dissemination in the houses, it is in business environment that Open Office the suite tests, tries the big bet, being able to already have several projects carried out in the public administration and in schools.
And there is no shortage of even the realities offered by an ideal training, consultation and assistance service for small and medium-sized businesses, in which business prospects could be opened.
Open Office is composed of five main modules: Writer, for the video write the corresponding of Word; Calc, it is the spreadsheet that replaces Excel; Impress, for the presentation of Powerpoint; Dbase, eats in the case of the well-known Access is the program that consents to work in the base data; and finally Draw the graphic module.
Goal for 2008 is to reach 5 million downloads, and considering that until today we reach almost 3 million 600 thousand, with the departure of the new version it is likely that the expected figure can be exceeded.
Kohl also proves positive is the fourth case of doping
New positive case in the tour of France: it is the Austrian Bernhard Kohl, team Gerolsteiner, third and winner of the best slander.
To give the news is the site of the newspaper L'Equipe.
Kohl, 26 years old is the fourth positive runner to the third-generation Epo, after the Italians Riccardo Riccò and Leonardo Piepoli and the German Stefan Schumacher, also they of the Gerolsteiner.
Analyses of Kohl’s blood champions come among those carried out in recent weeks in Losanna and Chatenay-Malabry’s lab.
If anti-test confirm that he is positive, the Austrian will lose third place to the Tour and anger against two years of canonical disqualification.
Confirming the news of Kohl’s positive doping of the third-generation Epo is the head of the French anti-doping agency, Pierre Bordry, who has told the Associated Press to have reported the news to the Austrian authorities.
The 26-year-old Austrian has positioned himself on the podium behind the backs of Carlos Sastre and American Cadel Evans, claiming the shirt of the best climber.
IMMIGRANTS: NEW YORK TIMES WONDERS, ITALY IS RACIST?
Italy as an emigrant country has only recently transformed into a privileged destination for immigrants" welcomed with hostility.
This is transforming the beautiful country into a nation of racists? Is what the New York Times wonders in a lengthy article that has devoted to the debate on the subject racism in Italy based on the case of the young Abdul William Guibre originally from Burkina Faso killed the previous month in Milan for having stolen a box of cookies.
